< ÍI:4Ω:UBÄºÜ˙ßº–`/Ωxà«º7Tº|Ñæºuº¿ç»<Sä=ÒÃ;?®Ó;WÜëª=Œ
ª9µº‰ÅŒº›7=É±x;è,␀Ω˙Ì;KØ°<␀Ú∫<™†ºós<+∑=\R≈<#˘=:•<◊˜=7Õı9gòÎºq>òºl7º¸9º0É∆º‚w'ªKbi:®p≤<pÁ8<}<C+àªX≠≠ºjƒ•=˘m!<ãåÒ:˛v<ú∂∑;e°í<?/ëº‰ª8<Û˝’º‚=£\<¯P¨ºÉXº¡º,∆ª?Lºﬂ“Ω‹√ <†xDº—;˚û‰<z÷;,∆ºE≤<àœ:pÁ8<Å◊º_†˝;A Ω0ÉF;lÎAªª:r<úë;‘?1<d-æ;~<$;õ¨êªøÙ;/I\ºQ=$ +;_ΩÚº#~<*}(=…ø†<z@-º«{Ω„dŸ<g{vºQ)<◊˜ñº7q=S Ìº£Mü<ó∞º©«ëº†[OΩà!ƒºW9Ÿº"ø§º(ΩºlÎ¡;ÈÒ<ù*å<ï2û<{"title": "GEMELOS:Los gemelos son sujetos de un estudio que relaciona el tabaquismo con la enfermedad tiroidea autoinmune, mostrando la influencia gen\u00e9tica en la enfermedad."}{"title": "PRESENCIA DE ANTICUERPOS:La presencia de anticuerpos antihormonas tiroideas puede interferir con la determinaci\u00f3n anal\u00edtica de las hormonas tiroideas, aunque no est\u00e1 relacionada con la etiopatogenia de la enfermedad de Graves."}{"title": "OFTALMOPAT\u00cdA DE GRAVES:La oftalmopat\u00eda de Graves es una enfermedad inflamatoria ocular asociada con enfermedad tiroidea autoinmune, principalmente la enfermedad de Graves."}{"title": "HIPERTIROIDISMO:HIPERTIROIDISMO, or hyperthyroidism, is a medical condition characterized by the excessive production of thyroid hormones by the thyroid gland. This overproduction can lead to various metabolic disturbances and a range of symptoms, including gastrointestinal issues such as chronic diarrhea. Additionally, hyperthyroidism can influence levels of ferritin and increase sex hormone-binding globulin (SHBG) levels, which may affect testosterone availability.\n\nThe condition can be treated with radioiodine therapy, and it is important to note that hyperthyroidism is a contraindication for the use of certain medications, including fentermina and topiramato. Furthermore, hyperthyroidism may also arise as a potential adverse effect of immune checkpoint inhibitors, especially when these therapies are used in combination. Overall, hyperthyroidism is a significant health concern that requires careful management and treatment."}{"title": "EUROPEAN GROUP ON GRAVES' ORBITOPATHY:The European Group on Graves' Orbitopathy (EUGOGO) is a dedicated organization that focuses on the management and research of Graves' orbitopathy, a condition associated with thyroid disease. EUGOGO aims to establish consensus guidelines for the treatment and management of this condition, facilitating improved care and understanding among healthcare professionals across Europe."}{"title": "BAHN RS:Bahn RS es un autor que ha contribuido a la literatura m\u00e9dica sobre la oftalmopat\u00eda de Graves."}{"title": "MANDEL SJ:Mandel SJ is an author recognized for his contributions to the field of endocrinology, particularly in the areas of thyroiditis and hyperthyroidism, as evidenced by his writings in medical texts. He is notably one of the authors of the American Thyroid Association Management Guidelines for Adult Patients with Thyroid Nodules and Differentiated Thyroid Cancer, which serves as a significant resource for healthcare professionals managing these conditions."}{"title": "KAHALY GJ:Kahaly GJ es un investigador que ha realizado estudios sobre el tratamiento de la oftalmopat\u00eda de Graves."}{"title": "GRAVES:Graves is an autoimmune disorder that affects the thyroid gland, resulting in hyperthyroidism. This condition is characterized by the overactivity of the thyroid, which can lead to various symptoms associated with excessive thyroid hormone production. Additionally, Graves' disease is often linked with Graves' ophthalmopathy, a condition that affects the eyes and can cause symptoms such as bulging eyes and vision problems."}{"title": "AMIODARONE:Amiodarone is a medication primarily used to treat serious irregular heartbeats, functioning as an antiarrhythmic agent. It is widely recognized for its effectiveness in managing various cardiac conditions. Notably, amiodarone has a high iodine content, which can significantly impact thyroid function, potentially leading to conditions such as type 2 thyrotoxicosis. This dual effect on both cardiac rhythm and thyroid health underscores the importance of monitoring thyroid function in patients undergoing treatment with amiodarone."}{"title": "OSTEOCALCINA:Osteocalcina is a protein that plays a crucial role in evaluating bone health, particularly in patients with inflammatory bowel disease. It is produced by osteoblasts and functions as a hormone involved in bone formation. Additionally, osteocalcin levels can be elevated in conditions such as hyperthyroidism, indicating its significance in various metabolic processes related to bone health."}{"title": "SHBG:SHBG (Sex Hormone-Binding Globulin) is a protein that plays a crucial role in binding sex hormones, thereby regulating their availability and influencing hormone levels in the body, particularly testosterone. It serves as an important marker in diagnosing conditions such as thyroid hormone resistance and TSHomas. Additionally, SHBG levels are influenced by thyroid hormones, highlighting its interconnectedness with the endocrine system. Overall, SHBG is essential for maintaining hormonal balance and is significant in various clinical assessments related to hormone-related disorders."}{"title": "FERRITINA:Ferritina, also known as ferritin, is a crucial protein that stores iron in the body, playing a vital role in maintaining iron homeostasis and preventing anemia. It functions by releasing iron when needed, thus regulating iron levels within cells. Ferritin levels are commonly measured to evaluate the body's iron stores, which is particularly important for patients with eating disorders and those suffering from conditions such as hemochromatosis. Elevated ferritin levels can occur in various medical conditions, including hyperthyroidism and inflammatory bowel disease, even in cases of iron deficiency. Additionally, ferritin serves as a significant biomarker for assessing iron levels in the blood, making it an essential component in diagnosing and managing various health conditions related to iron metabolism."}{"title": "N\u00d3DULO T\u00d3XICO:Toxic nodules are hyperfunctioning thyroid nodules that can cause hyperthyroidism by producing excess thyroid hormones."}{"title": "TIROIDITIS DESTRUCTIVA:Tiroiditis destructiva is a type of thyroiditis that leads to the release of stored hormones rather than an increase in hormone synthesis."}{"title": "BERTALENA L:Bertalena L is a researcher who has contributed to the understanding of Graves' orbitopathy and its management."}{"title": "FIBROSIS DE LA MUSCULATURA OCULAR:Fibrosis de la musculatura ocular is a condition that can occur in the later stages of Graves' ophthalmopathy, characterized by scarring of the eye muscles."}{"title": "H\u00c1BITO TAB\u00c1QUICO:H\u00e1bito tab\u00e1quico, or the practice of smoking, is a significant factor that influences various health outcomes. It is particularly noted for its role in the progression of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD) and other respiratory diseases, making it a critical prognostic factor. In Spain, tobacco habits are a key determinant of the prevalence of COPD across different demographics. Additionally, smoking has been linked to an increased risk and severity of Graves' ophthalmopathy, highlighting its detrimental effects on overall health."}{"title": "RECEPTORES DE TSH:Receptores de TSH are thyroid-stimulating hormone receptors that play a role in the regulation of thyroid function and are implicated in autoimmune conditions like Graves' disease."}{"title": "ECO-DOPPLER TIROIDEA:"}{"title": "BARTALENA L:Bartalena L is a researcher who has contributed to the management of Graves' ophthalmopathy and has published multiple studies on the subject."}{"title": "PINCHERA A:Pinchera A is a researcher involved in the study and management of Graves' ophthalmopathy, contributing to various publications."}{"title": "MARCOCCI C:Marcocci C is a researcher who has worked on the management of Graves' ophthalmopathy and has authored several relevant studies."}{"title": "HEGEDUS L:Hegedus L is a researcher known for his work on the relationship between cigarette smoking and Graves' ophthalmopathy. Additionally, he is one of the authors of the American Association of Clinical Endocrinologists Medical Guidelines for Clinical Practice, which focuses on the diagnosis and management of thyroid nodules."}{"title": "BRATINAS:Bratinas is a nationality mentioned in the context of individuals affected by Graves' disease, particularly in relation to environmental factors."}{"title": "YERSINIA ENTEROCOLITICA:Yersinia enterocolitica is a bacterium implicated in the environmental factors contributing to Graves' disease."}{"title": "THYROID:The thyroid is a gland located in the neck that plays a crucial role in the body's metabolism by producing hormones. It can develop nodules, which may be either benign or malignant. Diseases of the thyroid are often classified and staged according to the American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) guidelines. Additionally, \"Thyroid\" is a medical journal dedicated to publishing research related to thyroid diseases and disorders. This journal covers a wide range of topics, including guidelines and studies on specific conditions such as medullary thyroid carcinoma and Graves' disease, along with their complications and treatments. Overall, the thyroid is a vital gland with significant implications for health, and ongoing research in the field is essential for understanding and managing thyroid-related conditions."}{"title": "GRAVES' DISEASE:Graves' disease is an autoimmune disorder that is recognized as the most common cause of hyperthyroidism, particularly in adults. This condition affects the thyroid gland, resulting in an overproduction of thyroid hormones. In addition to hyperthyroidism, Graves' disease can lead to various complications, one of the most notable being Graves' orbitopathy, which affects the eyes."}{"title": "METHYLPREDNISOLONE:Methylprednisolone is a corticosteroid medication used in the treatment of Graves' orbitopathy to reduce inflammation."}{"title": "LIVER DAMAGE:Liver damage is a potential side effect associated with the use of intravenous glucocorticoid pulse therapy in patients with Graves' orbitopathy."}{"title": "CIGARETTE SMOKING:Cigarette smoking has been identified as an environmental factor that may exacerbate Graves' ophthalmopathy."}{"title": "STRESS EMOTIONAL:Emotional stress is considered a potential environmental trigger for the onset or exacerbation of Graves' disease."}{"title": "IODINE:IODINE is a mineral that plays a crucial role in thyroid function, and its dietary intake is subject to specific recommendations. It is essential for the production of thyroid hormones, which regulate various metabolic processes in the body. The dietary reference intake for iodine, also referred to as \"Yodo,\" varies across different age groups, as outlined in dietary guidelines. However, it is important to note that excessive iodine consumption has been linked to the development of Graves' disease, an autoimmune disorder that affects the thyroid. Therefore, while iodine is vital for health, maintaining an appropriate balance in dietary intake is essential to prevent potential health issues."}{"title": "GRAVES' ORBITOPATHY:"}{"title": "BECK-PECCOZ P:Beck-Peccoz P is a prominent researcher in the field of endocrinology, particularly known for their contributions to the European Thyroid Association Guidelines for the Diagnosis and Treatment of Thyrotropin-Secreting Pituitary Tumors. This researcher has played a significant role in developing these guidelines, which are essential for diagnosing and treating TSH-secreting pituitary tumors. Additionally, Beck-Peccoz P has contributed to the broader understanding of thyroid hormone action and its associated disorders, further establishing their expertise and influence in the field."}{"title": "LANIA A:Lania A is a co-author and researcher involved in the European Thyroid Association Guidelines for the Diagnosis and Treatment of Thyrotropin-Secreting Pituitary Tumors. Her work is focused on endocrinology research, contributing to the development of guidelines that aid in the diagnosis and treatment of these specific pituitary tumors."}{"title": "BECKERS A:Beckers A is a notable researcher and co-author of the European Thyroid Association Guidelines for the Diagnosis and Treatment of Thyrotropin-Secreting Pituitary Tumors. Through this work, Beckers A has significantly contributed to the understanding of TSHomas, enhancing the guidelines that inform the diagnosis and treatment of these specific pituitary tumors."}{"title": "CHATTERJEE K:Chatterjee K is a prominent researcher and co-author of the European Thyroid Association Guidelines for the Diagnosis and Treatment of Thyrotropin-Secreting Pituitary Tumors. This individual is actively involved in clinical research and has made significant contributions to the understanding of thyroid hormone action and related disorders. Through their work, Chatterjee K has played a vital role in advancing knowledge and guidelines pertaining to thyroid health and its associated conditions."}{"title": "WEMEAU J-L:Wemeau J-L is a researcher who contributed to the European Thyroid Association Guidelines for the Diagnosis and Treatment of Thyrotropin-Secreting Pituitary Tumors."}{"title": "OLATEJU TO:Olateju TO is a researcher who studied thyroid hormone resistance."}{"title": "VANDERPUMP MP:Vanderpump MP is a researcher who studied thyroid hormone resistance."}{"title": "SINGHN BK:Singhn BK is a researcher who provided insights into thyroid hormone resistance due to receptor mutations."}{"title": "YEN PM:Yen PM is a researcher who provided insights into thyroid hormone resistance due to receptor mutations."}{"title": "CRISIS TIROT\u00d3XICA:Crisis tirot\u00f3xica is a rare clinical condition characterized by exacerbated hyperthyroidism symptoms and has a significant mortality rate."}{"title": "EUROPEAN THYROID ASSOCIATION GUIDELINES:"}{"title": "THYROID HORMONE RESISTANCE:Thyroid hormone resistance is a condition characterized by the body's tissues exhibiting resistance to the effects of thyroid hormones. This resistance results in a range of clinical challenges, impacting the overall functioning of the endocrine system and potentially leading to various health issues."}{"title": "MUTACI\u00d3N EN EL GEN DEL RECEPTOR DE HORMONAS TIROIDEAS:Mutaci\u00f3n en el gen del receptor de hormonas tiroideas refers to genetic mutations that affect the body's response to thyroid hormones."}{"title": "TIROTROPINOMA:"}{"title": "JAPAN THYROID ASSOCIATION:The Japan Thyroid Association is a professional organization focused on thyroid health, involved in establishing diagnostic criteria and guidelines for thyroid-related conditions."}{"title": "JAPAN ENDOCRINE SOCIETY:The Japan Endocrine Society is a professional organization that collaborates with the Japan Thyroid Association on endocrine health issues, including thyroid storm management."}{"title": "THYROID STORM:Thyroid storm is a severe and life-threatening condition resulting from uncontrolled hyperthyroidism, requiring immediate medical attention and management."}{"title": "TIAMAZOL:Tiamazol is a medication utilized for the treatment of hyperthyroidism, primarily by inhibiting the production of thyroid hormones. It is classified as an antithyroid medication and is noted for its potential teratogenic effects, which are important considerations in the context of thyroid treatment. In particular situations, such as during pregnancy, Tiamazol may be switched to another medication known as PTU to mitigate risks associated with its use."}{"title": "PROPYLTHIOURACIL (PTU):Propylthiouracil (PTU) is a medication used to manage hyperthyroidism, particularly during the first trimester of pregnancy due to its lower teratogenic risk compared to tiamazol."}{"title": "T4L:T4L refers to free thyroxine levels, which are important for assessing thyroid function, especially during pregnancy."}{"title": "THYROID DISEASE:Thyroid disease refers to various conditions affecting the thyroid gland, including hypothyroidism and hyperthyroidism, which can be influenced by medications like amiodarone."}{"title": "HYPERTIROIDISM:Hyperthyroidism is a medical condition characterized by the excessive production of thyroid hormones by an overactive thyroid gland. This condition can manifest in various forms, including subclinical hyperthyroidism, which may necessitate treatment depending on specific patient factors, particularly in older adults. Additionally, hyperthyroidism can be associated with other endocrine disorders. It is important to note that hyperthyroidism can also be induced as a side effect of certain medications, such as amiodarone, which can significantly affect thyroid function."}{"title": "TIROCYTE:Tirocytes are the cells of the thyroid gland that can be affected by drugs like amiodarone, leading to cytotoxic effects."}{"title": "AMERICAN THYROID ASSOCIATION:The American Thyroid Association (ATA) is a professional organization dedicated to advancing the understanding and management of thyroid diseases. It provides comprehensive guidelines and recommendations for the diagnosis and treatment of various thyroid conditions, including thyroid nodules, differentiated thyroid cancer, and medullary thyroid carcinoma. The ATA's guidelines also encompass the management of thyroid disease during pregnancy and the postpartum period, ensuring that both patients and healthcare providers have access to the latest research and best practices in thyroid health. Through its efforts, the American Thyroid Association plays a crucial role in improving patient outcomes and promoting awareness of thyroid-related health issues."}{"title": "PROPILTHIOURACIL:Propylthiouracil (PTU) is a medication used to treat hyperthyroidism, particularly during pregnancy, as recommended by the American Thyroid Association."}{"title": "PEARCE EN:Pearce EN is one of the authors of the 2017 Guidelines of the American Thyroid Association for the Diagnosis and Management of Thyroid Disease During Pregnancy and the Postpartum."}{"title": "BROWN RS:Brown RS is a significant contributor and one of the authors of the 2017 Guidelines of the American Thyroid Association for the Diagnosis and Management of Thyroid Disease During Pregnancy and the Postpartum."}{"title": "CHEN H:Chen H is a prominent researcher known for significant contributions to medical guidelines in the field of endocrinology. Notably, Chen H played a key role in developing the consensus guideline for the diagnosis and management of neuroendocrine tumors. Additionally, Chen H is recognized as one of the authors of the 2017 Guidelines of the American Thyroid Association, which focus on the diagnosis and management of thyroid disease during pregnancy and the postpartum period. Through these contributions, Chen H has made a substantial impact on the standards of care in these areas of medicine."}{"title": "DOSIOU C:Dosiou C is a co-author of the 2017 Guidelines of the American Thyroid Association for the Diagnosis and Management of Thyroid Disease During Pregnancy and the Postpartum. This involvement highlights Dosiou C's significant contribution to the field of thyroid disease management, particularly in relation to pregnancy and the postpartum period."}{"title": "ANDERSEN SL:Andersen SL is one of the authors of the study on the severity of birth defects after propylthiouracil exposure in early pregnancy."}{"title": "OLSEN J:Olsen J is one of the authors of the study on the severity of birth defects after propylthiouracil exposure in early pregnancy."}{"title": "WU CS:Wu CS is one of the authors of the study on the severity of birth defects after propylthiouracil exposure in early pregnancy."}{"title": "LAURBERG P:Laurberg P is a notable figure in the field of endocrinology, recognized for co-authoring a textbook that emphasizes hyperthyroid disorders. Additionally, Laurberg P contributed to research examining the severity of birth defects associated with propylthiouracil exposure during early pregnancy. This work highlights Laurberg P's involvement in both educational and research initiatives within the medical community, particularly concerning thyroid health and its implications for maternal and fetal well-being."}{"title": "AZIZI F:Azizi F is one of the authors of the study on thyroid function and intellectual development of infants nursed by mothers taking methimazole."}{"title": "KHOSHNIAT M:Khoshniat M is one of the authors of the study on thyroid function and intellectual development of infants nursed by mothers taking methimazole."}{"title": "BAHRAINIAN M:Bahrainian M is one of the authors of the study on thyroid function and intellectual development of infants nursed by mothers taking methimazole."}{"title": "HEDAYATI M:Hedayati M is one of the authors of the study on thyroid function and intellectual development of infants nursed by mothers taking methimazole."}{"title": "JOHANSEN K:Johansen K is one of the authors of the study on the excretion of methimazole in human milk."}{"title": "ANDERSON SL:Anderson SL is one of the authors of the study on the use of antithyroid drugs in pregnancy and lactation."}{"title": "MARTINO E:Martino E is a researcher known for his contributions to the field of endocrinology, particularly in relation to thyroid health. He has published studies examining the effects of amiodarone on the thyroid, highlighting the drug's impact on thyroid function. Additionally, Martino E is one of the authors of a study that explores the use of antithyroid drugs during pregnancy and lactation, further demonstrating his involvement in important research concerning thyroid treatment in vulnerable populations."}{"title": "MAMMOLI C:Mammoli C is one of the authors of the study on the in vitro cytotoxic effect of amiodarone."}{"title": "CHIOVATO L:Chiovato L is one of the authors of the study on the in vitro cytotoxic effect of amiodarone."}{"title": "HARJAI KJ:Harjai KJ is a researcher known for studying the effects of amiodarone on thyroid function. In addition to conducting this research, Harjai KJ is also one of the authors of the study that explores the impact of amiodarone on thyroid function."}{"title": "LICATA AA:Licata AA is a researcher known for collaborating with Harjai KJ on a study investigating the effects of amiodarone on thyroid function. In addition to this collaboration, Licata AA is recognized as one of the authors of the study, contributing to the understanding of how amiodarone impacts thyroid health."}{"title": "ALEXANDER EK:Alexander EK is a notable researcher recognized for his contributions to the field of thyroid disease, particularly in the context of pregnancy and postpartum care. He played a significant role in developing guidelines for the diagnosis and management of thyroid disease during these critical periods. Additionally, Alexander EK is one of the authors of the American Thyroid Association Management Guidelines for Adult Patients with Thyroid Nodules and Differentiated Thyroid Cancer, further highlighting his expertise and influence in the management of thyroid-related health issues."}{"title": "PITSIVAS V:Pitsiavas V is a researcher who studied the ultrastructural changes in the thyroid due to amiodarone."}{"title": "TRIP MD:Trip MD is a researcher who investigated the incidence and pathogenesis of amiodarone-induced thyrotoxicosis and hypothyroidism."}{"title": "ENDOCRINOLOGY:Endocrinology is a specialized branch of medicine that focuses on the endocrine system, its diseases, and the hormones it produces. This field plays a crucial role in the management of various health conditions, particularly diabetes, and is also involved in nutrition management. Endocrinology encompasses the study of specific secretions known as hormones, which are vital for numerous bodily functions. Additionally, the field includes research published in medical journals, such as studies on the cytotoxic effects of amiodarone and discussions on related disorders, including those concerning carcinoid tumors as noted by \u00d6berg KE. Overall, endocrinology is essential for understanding and treating hormonal imbalances and related health issues."}{"title": "ANN INTERN MED:Ann Intern Med, also known as the Annals of Internal Medicine, is a peer-reviewed medical journal that focuses on publishing research and reviews in the field of internal medicine. The journal covers a wide range of topics, including the effects of various health interventions, such as dietary impacts on diabetes and the effects of amiodarone on thyroid function. Through its publications, Ann Intern Med contributes to the advancement of medical knowledge and practice by disseminating important findings related to internal medicine and health interventions."}{"title": "ARCH INTERN MED:ARCH INTERN MED, also known as Archives of Internal Medicine, is a prominent medical journal dedicated to publishing research and systematic reviews in the field of internal medicine. The journal covers a wide range of topics, including studies on frailty, nutrition in older adults, cardiovascular disease, and specific medical conditions such as amiodarone-induced hypothyroidism. Additionally, it explores the relationship between frailty and various physiological systems, including inflammation and coagulation. Through its diverse array of published research, ARCH INTERN MED contributes significantly to the understanding and advancement of internal medicine."}{"title": "EUR J ENDOCRINOL:Eur J Endocrinol, also known as the European Journal of Endocrinology, is a medical journal dedicated to publishing research in the field of endocrinology. It features studies on various topics, including the effects of amiodarone in rats, highlighting its focus on both clinical and experimental research within endocrinology. The journal serves as a platform for disseminating significant findings and advancements in the understanding of endocrine disorders and treatments."}{"title": "AM J MED:AM J MED, also known as the American Journal of Medicine, is a peer-reviewed medical journal that publishes a diverse array of articles covering a wide range of medical topics. The journal is known for its contributions to the field, including studies on specific medical conditions such as amiodarone-induced thyrotoxicosis and hypothyroidism. It serves as a platform for research articles, reviews, and meta-analyses, making it a significant resource for medical professionals and researchers."}{"title": "CARBIMAZOL:Carbimazol is another antithyroid medication that can have teratogenic effects, mentioned in the context of thyroid treatment."}{"title": "PROPILTIURACILO:Propiltiuracilo (PTU) is an antithyroid medication that can have hepatotoxic effects and is used during pregnancy."}{"title": "GRAVES DISEASE:Graves disease is the most common cause of hyperthyroidism during pregnancy, affecting thyroid function."}{"title": "TSI:TSI (thyroid-stimulating immunoglobulins) are antibodies that can cross the placenta and cause transient hyperthyroidism in the fetus."}{"title": "FETAL MALFORMATIONS:Fetal malformations can occur due to exposure to antithyroid medications like tiamazol during pregnancy."}{"title": "DANISH NATIONWIDE STUDY:A study conducted in Denmark examining birth defects after early pregnancy use of antithyroid drugs."}{"title": "HYPERTHYROIDISM:A medical condition characterized by excessive thyroid hormone production, which can affect pregnancy."}{"title": "LIVER TRANSPLANTATION:Liver transplantation is a surgical procedure that involves replacing a diseased liver with a healthy liver from a donor. This procedure is often necessary for patients suffering from end-stage liver disease, which can result from various conditions, including drug-induced liver injury. The process aims to restore normal liver function and improve the patient's quality of life."}{"title": "FETAL AND NEONATAL HYPERTHYROIDISM:A condition where a fetus or newborn has excessive thyroid hormone levels, which can lead to various health issues."}{"title": "MCT8:A protein that is involved in the cellular transport of thyroid hormones, mutations of which can lead to neurological deficiencies."}{"title": "SECISBP2:A selenoprotein involved in the metabolism of thyroid hormones, mutations of which can affect hormone conversion."}{"title": "DUMITRESCU AM:Dumitrescu AM is an author of research related to mutations affecting thyroid hormone metabolism."}{"title": "LAO XH:Liao XH is a co-author of research on thyroid hormone metabolism and its mutations."}{"title": "SINGH BK:Singh BK is mentioned in the context of thyroid hormone research and its implications."}{"title": "BECK-PECCOZ:Beck-Peccoz is a researcher who has contributed to the understanding of thyroid hormone action and its disorders, including TSH-secreting pituitary tumors."}{"title": "LANIA:Lania is a researcher involved in the European Thyroid Association Guidelines for the diagnosis and treatment of thyroid disorders."}{"title": "BECKERS:Beckers is a researcher who has published work on thyroid hormone action and related disorders."}{"title": "CHATTERJEE:Chatterjee is a researcher who has contributed to the field of endocrinology, particularly in thyroid hormone resistance."}{"title": "WEMEAU:Wemeau is a researcher involved in the study of pituitary tumors and thyroid hormone action."}{"title": "TSHOMA:TSHoma refers to a type of pituitary tumor characterized by its production and secretion of excess thyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH). This condition is the focus of various studies and clinical evaluations, highlighting its significance in understanding pituitary tumors and their effects on hormone regulation."}{"title": "RHT:RHT, which stands for Resistance to Hormones Thyroid (or resistencia a hormonas tiroideas in Spanish), is a medical condition characterized by the body's tissues failing to respond appropriately to thyroid hormones. This condition can be distinguished from TSHomas, a type of tumor that affects thyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH) levels, through specific tests and evaluations."}{"title": "EUROPEAN THYROID ASSOCIATION:The European Thyroid Association is an organization dedicated to advancing the understanding and treatment of thyroid disorders. It plays a crucial role in providing guidelines and conducting research related to these conditions. Among its contributions, the Association has developed specific guidelines for ultrasound malignancy risk stratification of thyroid nodules in adults, ensuring that healthcare professionals have the necessary resources to assess and manage thyroid health effectively."}{"title": "CLIN DIABETES ENDOCRINOL:Clin Diabetes Endocrinol is a scientific journal that focuses on research related to diabetes and endocrinology."}{"title": "BASSETT JH:Bassett JH is a researcher who has published work on thyroid hormone action and its disorders."}{"title": "BERNAL J:Bernal J is a researcher known for work in the field of thyroid hormone action."}{"title": "BRENT G:Brent G is a researcher who has published work on thyroid hormone action and its disorders."}{"title": "AM J HUM GENET:"}{"title": "TIROIDITIS DE RIEDEL:Tiroiditis de Riedel is a rare and chronic inflammatory disease of the thyroid gland, characterized by the presence of fibrosis within the thyroid tissue. This condition can lead to progressive local symptoms and may result in complications, including hypoparathyroidism. The fibrosis associated with Tiroiditis de Riedel can significantly affect thyroid function and overall health."}{"title": "HASHIMOTO:Hashimoto's thyroiditis is an autoimmune disorder that causes chronic inflammation of the thyroid gland, differing from Riedel's in that it does not involve fibrosis."}{"title": "MAYO CLINIC:The Mayo Clinic is a renowned medical center that has conducted extensive research and treatment for various thyroid conditions, including Riedel's thyroiditis."}{"title": "BARTHOLOMEW LG:Bartholomew LG is an author of a study discussing the association of sclerosing cholangitis with Riedel's struma and fibrous retroperitonitis."}{"title": "FALHAMMAR H:Falhammar H is a researcher who has published findings on the clinical presentation, treatment, and outcomes of Riedel's thyroiditis."}{"title": "EGSGAARD NIELSEN V:Egsgaard Nielsen V is an author of a case report on a rare case of orbital involvement in Riedel's thyroiditis."}{"title": "TSH-SECRETING PITUITARY ADENOMAS:TSH-secreting pituitary adenomas are tumors that produce excess thyroid-stimulating hormone, which can lead to hyperthyroidism."}{"title": "CLINICAL GUIDELINES:Clinical guidelines are systematically developed statements designed to assist both practitioners and patients in making informed decisions regarding appropriate healthcare for specific clinical circumstances. These guidelines encompass a wide range of medical conditions and provide evidence-based recommendations tailored for healthcare professionals. For instance, clinical guidelines for the management of amyotrophic lateral sclerosis offer targeted recommendations to improve patient care. Additionally, they include protocols for the diagnosis and treatment of conditions such as incidental pituitary adenomas, as well as management strategies for hyponatremia, addressing various severity levels. Overall, clinical guidelines serve as a crucial resource in ensuring effective and standardized healthcare practices."}{"title": "PITUITARY TUMOR:"}{"title": "FALHAMMAR ET AL.:Falhammar et al. es un grupo de investigadores que realizaron una serie reciente sobre la tiroiditis de Riedel, presentando datos sobre la positividad de anticuerpos en pacientes."}{"title": "KAKUDO ET AL.:Kakudo et al. es un grupo de investigadores que estudiaron el diagn\u00f3stico de la tiroiditis de Hashimoto y la enfermedad esclerosante relacionada con IgG4."}{"title": "HENNESSEY JV.:Hennessey JV. es un autor que realiz\u00f3 una revisi\u00f3n cl\u00ednica sobre la tiroiditis de Riedel, abordando su presentaci\u00f3n y tratamiento."}{"title": "HARTEMANN ET AL.:Hartemann et al. es un grupo de investigadores que documentaron un caso de tiroiditis de Riedel regresiva."}{"title": "CIBAS ES:Cibas ES is an author who has significantly contributed to the development of the Bethesda system for the classification and reporting of thyroid cytology. Their work has been instrumental in enhancing the standards and practices related to thyroid cytopathology, providing a structured approach for the evaluation and communication of cytological findings."}{"title": "CAMPANELLA ET AL.:Campanella et al. conducted a comprehensive meta-analysis examining the cancer risk linked to both clinical and ultrasonographic features of thyroid nodules. Their research focused on identifying factors associated with malignancy in these nodules, utilizing a thorough evaluation of the ultrasonographic characteristics. This study contributes valuable insights into the assessment of thyroid nodules and their potential cancer risk."}{"title": "BETHESDA SYSTEM:The Bethesda System is a classification system specifically designed for reporting thyroid cytopathology. It offers comprehensive guidelines for the management of thyroid nodules and cancer, facilitating standardized communication and decision-making in clinical practice."}{"title": "CAMPANELLA:Campanella is a researcher who conducted a study on the malignancy risk of thyroid nodules, providing odds ratios for various characteristics associated with malignancy."}{"title": "BRITO:Brito is a researcher who conducted a meta-analysis on the accuracy of thyroid nodule ultrasound to predict thyroid cancer."}{"title": "REMONTI:Remonti is a researcher who authored a meta-analysis on thyroid ultrasound features and the risk of carcinoma."}{"title": "EU-TIRADS:EU-TIRADS is a classification system used to categorize the risk of malignancy in thyroid nodules based on ultrasound features."}{"title": "THYROID NODULES:Thyroid nodules are abnormal growths that occur in the thyroid gland, which can be either benign or malignant. The characteristics of these nodules are assessed to evaluate the risk of cancer. Their management is guided by the American Thyroid Association, ensuring that appropriate monitoring or treatment is provided based on the specific circumstances of each case. Overall, thyroid nodules may require careful observation or intervention depending on their nature and associated risks."}{"title": "THYROID CANCER:Thyroid cancer is a type of cancer that occurs in the thyroid gland, which can be predicted through ultrasound features of thyroid nodules."}{"title": "MICROCALCIFICATIONS:Microcalcifications are small deposits of calcium in the thyroid nodules that are associated with a higher risk of malignancy."}{"title": "MARGINS IRREGULARES:Irregular margins of thyroid nodules are a characteristic that indicates a higher risk of malignancy."}{"title": "HIPOECOGENICIDAD:Hypoechogenicity refers to the appearance of thyroid nodules on ultrasound, which can be associated with malignancy."}{"title": "ANALYSIS:Analysis refers to the systematic review and evaluation of thyroid nodules and their characteristics in relation to cancer risk."}{"title": "PAAF:PAAF, or Punci\u00f3n Aspiraci\u00f3n con Aguja Fina, is a medical procedure utilized for diagnostic purposes. It is primarily employed to evaluate thyroid nodules and assess the potential for malignancy. Additionally, PAAF is also performed to obtain tissue samples from liver lesions, aiding in the diagnosis of various conditions. This technique is significant in the medical field for its role in determining the nature of suspicious lesions in both the thyroid and liver."}{"title": "CATEGOR\u00cdA BETHESDA:El sistema Bethesda es una clasificaci\u00f3n de hallazgos citol\u00f3gicos en PAAF de n\u00f3dulos tiroideos que categoriza el riesgo de malignidad."}{"title": "VANDERPAS J.:Vanderpas J. es un autor que ha escrito sobre epidemiolog\u00eda nutricional y metabolismo de hormonas tiroideas."}{"title": "BALOCH ZW:Baloch ZW es un autor que ha contribuido a la terminolog\u00eda diagn\u00f3stica y criterios morfol\u00f3gicos para el diagn\u00f3stico citol\u00f3gico de lesiones tiroideas."}{"title": "HAUGEN BR:Haugen BR is a prominent author who has significantly contributed to the field of thyroid health, particularly in the development of management guidelines for thyroid conditions. He is recognized as one of the authors of the American Thyroid Association Management Guidelines for Adult Patients with Thyroid Nodules and Differentiated Thyroid Cancer, specifically the 2015 edition. His work focuses on providing comprehensive guidance for the management of thyroid nodules and differentiated thyroid cancer, reflecting his expertise and commitment to improving patient care in this area."}{"title": "NABO:NABO, known as \"nabo\" in Spanish, is a vegetable that possesses certain properties relevant to health. It contains substances that may interfere with the uptake of iodine by thyroid cells, which is an important consideration for individuals concerned about thyroid function. Additionally, NABO has a low galactose content, measuring less than 5 mg per 100 grams, making it a suitable option for those monitoring their galactose intake."}{"title": "BR\u00d3COLI:Br\u00f3coli is a vegetable that is notable for its nutritional content. It contains a moderate amount of galactose, ranging from 5 to 10 mg per 100 grams. Additionally, br\u00f3coli is known to contain thiocyanates, which have the potential to inhibit the uptake of iodine by thyroid cells. This dual aspect of br\u00f3coli highlights both its nutritional benefits and its possible effects on thyroid function."}{"title": "ALMENDRAS:Almendras, or almonds, are a type of nut recognized for their numerous health benefits and versatility in culinary applications. They are particularly noted for being a significant source of magnesium, which is essential for various bodily functions. Additionally, almonds are classified as a type of dried fruit that does not contain thiocyanates, meaning they do not interfere with iodine uptake by the thyroid gland. This makes them a healthy choice for those concerned about thyroid function. Overall, almendras are valued for their nutritional properties and their role in a balanced diet."}{"title": "AR\u00c1NDANOS:AR\u00c1NDANOS, commonly known as blueberries, are fruits that are notable for their nutritional properties. They contain oxalate, a compound that can contribute to the risk of kidney stone formation. However, it is important to note that blueberries do not contain thiocyanates, which means they do not affect the uptake of iodine by thyroid cells (tirocitos). This makes them a safe choice for individuals concerned about iodine absorption while still providing the health benefits associated with their consumption."}{"title": "COL:"}{"title": "BONGIOVANNI ET AL.:Bongiovanni et al. are researchers who conducted a meta-analysis on the Bethesda System for Reporting Thyroid Cytopathology."}{"title": "CIBAS ET AL.:Cibas et al. are researchers who contributed to the Bethesda System for Reporting Thyroid Cytopathology."}{"title": "HAUGEN ET AL.:Haugen et al. are authors of the 2015 American Thyroid Association Management Guidelines for Adult Patients with Thyroid Nodules and Differentiated Thyroid Cancer."}{"title": "THYROID NODULE:Thyroid nodules are growths in the thyroid gland that may require evaluation and management based on their characteristics and risk of malignancy."}{"title": "PUNCION ASPIRATIVA CON AGUJA FINA:Fine-needle aspiration (FNA) is a procedure used to obtain a sample from a thyroid nodule for cytological evaluation to determine the risk of malignancy."}{"title": "CANCER DIFERENCIADO DE TIROIDES:C\u00e1ncer diferenciado de tiroides refers to a group of thyroid cancers that are typically well-differentiated, primarily including papillary and follicular thyroid cancers. This type of cancer arises from follicular cells and is generally managed according to established guidelines, such as those provided by the American Thyroid Association."}{"title": "GU\u00cdA ATA 2015:The \"Gu\u00eda ATA 2015\" refers to the 2015 American Thyroid Association guidelines, which offer comprehensive recommendations for the management of thyroid nodules and differentiated thyroid cancer. These guidelines are designed to assist healthcare professionals in making informed decisions regarding the diagnosis, treatment, and follow-up of patients with these thyroid conditions."}{"title": "NODULO TIROIDEO:NODULO TIROIDEO refers to a thyroid nodule, which is a growth that occurs within the thyroid gland. These nodules can be assessed for the potential presence of malignancy by examining their characteristics through ultrasound imaging."}{"title": "AMERICAN ASSOCIATION OF CLINICAL ENDOCRINOLOGISTS:The American Association of Clinical Endocrinologists (AACE) is a professional organization dedicated to advancing the field of endocrinology. AACE plays a crucial role in developing comprehensive clinical practice guidelines that assist healthcare professionals in the diagnosis and management of various endocrine disorders. This includes providing guidelines for the diagnosis and management of thyroid nodules and related conditions, as well as offering consensus statements on diabetes management. Additionally, AACE focuses on the medical care of patients with obesity, ensuring that practitioners have access to the latest recommendations and best practices in this area. Through these efforts, AACE aims to enhance the quality of care for patients with endocrine-related health issues."}{"title": "NATIONAL COMPREHENSIVE CANCER NETWORK:The National Comprehensive Cancer Network (NCCN) is an organization dedicated to developing clinical practice guidelines in the field of oncology. Among its various contributions, the NCCN provides specific guidelines for the treatment and management of thyroid carcinoma. These guidelines are designed to assist healthcare professionals in delivering high-quality care to patients with cancer."}{"title": "KOREAN SOCIETY OF THYROID RADIOLOGY:The Korean Society of Thyroid Radiology provides consensus statements and recommendations for the ultrasonography diagnosis and management of thyroid nodules."}{"title": "BENNEDBAEK FN:Bennedbaek FN is a researcher involved in the treatment of recurrent thyroid cysts and has contributed to clinical studies."}{"title": "HEGED\u00dcS L:Heged\u00fcs L is a researcher and clinician who has contributed to guidelines and studies regarding thyroid nodules and their management."}{"title": "GHARIB H:Gharib H is a medical professional recognized for his contributions to the field of endocrinology, particularly in the management of thyroid nodules. He has co-authored guidelines that are instrumental in the diagnosis and management of these conditions. Notably, Gharib H is one of the authors of the American Association of Clinical Endocrinologists Medical Guidelines for Clinical Practice, which provides comprehensive recommendations for healthcare providers dealing with thyroid nodules."}{"title": "HADDAD RI:Haddad RI is a contributor to the NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology for thyroid carcinoma."}{"title": "NA DG:Na DG is a researcher who has published on radiofrequency ablation of benign thyroid nodules and recurrent thyroid cancers."}{"title": "PERROS P:Perros P is a medical professional who plays a significant role in the development of guidelines for the management of thyroid cancer. They are recognized as an author of the Guidelines for the management of thyroid cancer, which were published in the journal Clin Endocrinol. Through their contributions, Perros P has helped shape the standards and practices for treating this condition."}{"title": "VERDE G:Verde G is a researcher who has studied ultrasound-guided percutaneous ethanol injection in the treatment of cystic thyroid nodules."}{"title": "PUNCI\u00d3N ASPIRATIVA CON AGUJA FINA:Fine-needle aspiration (PAAF) is a procedure recommended for evaluating thyroid nodules suspected of malignancy."}{"title": "BOCIO DIFUSO NO T\u00d3XICO:BOCIO DIFUSO NO T\u00d3XICO, or diffuse non-toxic goiter, is a condition characterized by an enlarged thyroid gland that occurs without the presence of toxic symptoms. This condition is often associated with iodine deficiency or other factors that impede the synthesis of thyroid hormones. It represents an adaptive process of the thyroid in response to these challenges, reflecting the gland's efforts to maintain hormonal balance despite the difficulties in hormone production."}{"title": "DEFICIENCIA DE YODO:La deficiencia de yodo es un factor limitante en la s\u00edntesis de hormonas tiroideas y se asocia con la presencia de bocio en la poblaci\u00f3n."}{"title": "PUNCI\u00d3N ASPIRATIVA CON AGUJA FINA (PAAF):La PAAF es un procedimiento utilizado en el estudio de n\u00f3dulos tiroideos basado en su tama\u00f1o y sospecha de malignidad."}{"title": "N\u00d3DULO TIROIDEO:"}{"title": "TIRADS:The Thyroid Imaging Reporting and Data System (TIRADS) is a system used to stratify the risk of malignancy in thyroid nodules based on ultrasound features."}{"title": "BIBLE KC:Bible KC is an author who has contributed to the American Thyroid Association Management Guidelines for Adult Patients with Thyroid Nodules and Differentiated Thyroid Cancer."}{"title": "DOHERTY GM:Doherty GM is an author of the American Thyroid Association Management Guidelines for Adult Patients with Thyroid Nodules and Differentiated Thyroid Cancer. This involvement highlights Doherty GM's significant contribution to the field of thyroid health, particularly in providing evidence-based recommendations for the management of thyroid nodules and differentiated thyroid cancer in adult patients."}{"title": "NIKIFOROV YE:Nikiforov YE is an author of the American Thyroid Association Management Guidelines for Adult Patients with Thyroid Nodules and Differentiated Thyroid Cancer. He has contributed to the development of these guidelines, which serve as a critical resource for the management of thyroid conditions in adult patients."}{"title": "PAPINI E:Papini E is one of the authors of the American Association of Clinical Endocrinologists Medical Guidelines for Clinical Practice for the Diagnosis and Management of Thyroid Nodules."}{"title": "GARBER JR:Garber JR is one of the authors of the American Association of Clinical Endocrinologists Medical Guidelines for Clinical Practice for the Diagnosis and Management of Thyroid Nodules."}{"title": "DUICK DS:Duick DS is one of the authors of the American Association of Clinical Endocrinologists Medical Guidelines for Clinical Practice for the Diagnosis and Management of Thyroid Nodules."}{"title": "HARRELL RM:Harrell RM is one of the authors of the American Association of Clinical Endocrinologists Medical Guidelines for Clinical Practice for the Diagnosis and Management of Thyroid Nodules."}{"title": "THYROID IMAGING REPORTING AND DATA SYSTEM:The Thyroid Imaging Reporting and Data System (TIRADS) is a system used for stratifying cancer risk in thyroid nodules based on ultrasound features."}{"title": "BERTAGNA ET AL.:Bertagna et al. conducted a meta-analysis studying the frequency of malignancy in incidental thyroid lesions detected by 18F-FDG PET."}{"title": "SOELBERG ET AL.:Soelberg et al. published a meta-analysis on the risk of malignancy in thyroid incidentalomas detected by 18F-FDG PET."}{"title": "NAYAN ET AL.:Nayan et al. performed a systematic review and meta-analysis on the proportion of malignancy in incidental thyroid lesions on 18-FDG PET study."}{"title": "WHO:The World Health Organization (WHO) is a specialized agency of the United Nations dedicated to international public health. It plays a crucial role in providing guidelines and recommendations on various health-related topics, including alcohol consumption, nutrition, and health. The WHO is also involved in specific health management practices, such as providing formulas for calculating resting energy expenditure in patients, particularly in the context of managing cystic fibrosis. Additionally, the organization has made significant contributions to medical classifications, exemplified by its publication of a new classification of thyroid tumors in 2017, which introduced modifications to the previous classification. Furthermore, the WHO estimates the minimum amount of digestible carbohydrates necessary to prevent ketosis, highlighting its commitment to evidence-based health recommendations. Overall, the WHO's multifaceted approach underscores its vital role in shaping global health policies and practices."}{"title": "NIFTP:NIFTP stands for Non-Invasive Follicular Thyroid Neoplasm with Papillary-like nuclear features, a new category introduced in the WHO classification of thyroid tumors."}{"title": "EU-THYROID:The EU-Thyroid is a collaborative project that focuses on the management of thyroid diseases and the development of guidelines for thyroid care in Europe."}{"title": "CAMESSELLE-TEIJEIRO:Cameselle-Teijeiro is an author who contributed to the new WHO classification of thyroid tumors."}{"title": "LLOYD RV:Lloyd RV is a prominent researcher who plays a significant role in the development of the NANETS guidelines for neuroendocrine tumors. In addition to this, Lloyd RV serves as an editor for the WHO Classification of Tumours of Endocrine Organs, a comprehensive resource that encompasses various types of endocrine tumors, including those of the thyroid. Through these contributions, Lloyd RV is actively involved in advancing the understanding and classification of endocrine-related neoplasms."}{"title": "RADIOLGY:"}{"title": "IARC:The International Agency for Research on Cancer (IARC) is an intergovernmental agency that is part of the World Health Organization (WHO) and focuses on cancer research and classification."}{"title": "JAMA ONCOL:JAMA Oncology is a peer-reviewed medical journal that focuses on publishing research and reviews related to oncology and cancer treatment. The journal covers a wide range of topics within the field, including specific studies on various types of cancer, such as head and neck cancer."}{"title": "NCCN:The National Comprehensive Cancer Network (NCCN) is an alliance of leading cancer centers that develops guidelines for cancer care."}{"title": "THYROID CARCINOMA:Thyroid carcinoma is a type of cancer that originates in the thyroid gland, which is responsible for producing hormones that regulate metabolism and other bodily functions. This form of cancer is characterized by its various types, each requiring specific treatment protocols. Management of thyroid carcinoma is guided by established guidelines from organizations such as the National Comprehensive Cancer Network (NCCN) and the American Thyroid Association, which provide comprehensive recommendations for diagnosis, treatment, and follow-up care."}{"title": "HADDAD, RI:HADDAD, RI is a contributor to the NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology for Thyroid Carcinoma."}{"title": "SEETHALA, RR:RR Seethala is a researcher involved in the study and classification of thyroid tumors."}{"title": "NIKIFOROV, YE:YE Nikiforov is a prominent researcher in the field of thyroid cancer and its classification."}{"title": "2017:The year 2017 is significant as it marks the publication of the WHO Classification of Tumours of Endocrine Organs."}{"title": "NOMENCLATURE REVISION:The nomenclature revision for encapsulated follicular variant of papillary thyroid carcinoma represents a significant change in the classification to reduce overtreatment of indolent tumors."}{"title": "MOD PATHOL:Modern Pathology is a journal that publishes research related to pathology, including studies on thyroid neoplasms."}{"title": "SPENCER CA:Spencer CA is a researcher who has published work on the challenges of serum thyroglobulin measurement in the presence of Tg autoantibodies."}{"title": "COLLEY S:Colley S is an author of the Guidelines for the management of thyroid cancer published in Clin Endocrinol."}{"title": "EVANS C:Evans C is an author of the Guidelines for the management of thyroid cancer published in Clin Endocrinol."}{"title": "EVANS RM:Evans RM is an author of the Guidelines for the management of thyroid cancer published in Clin Endocrinol."}{"title": "GERRARD BA:Gerrard BA is an author of the Guidelines for the management of thyroid cancer published in Clin Endocrinol."}{"title": "GUIDELINES FOR THE MANAGEMENT OF THYROID CANCER:"}{"title": "CANCER TREAT REVIEWS:Cancer Treat Reviews is a journal that publishes critical reviews on cancer treatment, including syndromes like Cowden syndrome."}{"title": "JOURNAL OF GENETIC COUNSELING:The Journal of Genetic Counseling publishes research and reviews related to genetic counseling, including studies on Cowden syndrome."}{"title": "COWDEN SYNDROME:Cowden syndrome is a genetic condition associated with mutations in the PTEN gene, leading to an increased risk of various cancers."}{"title": "MEN2B:MEN2B is a genetic syndrome characterized by mutations in the RET proto-oncogene, leading to multiple endocrine neoplasia type 2B. This condition significantly increases the risk of developing medullary thyroid carcinoma, pheochromocytoma, and mucosal neuromas. MEN2B is recognized as the rarest and most aggressive form of multiple endocrine neoplasia type 2 (MEN2), with medullary thyroid carcinoma often manifesting in the first or second decade of life. Due to the high risk of these malignancies, early surgical intervention, specifically prophylactic thyroidectomy, is typically required for affected individuals. The syndrome is associated with distinct phenotypic features that further characterize its presentation."}{"title": "PTEN:PTEN is a tumor suppressor gene that plays a crucial role in regulating cell growth and apoptosis. It is particularly significant in the context of Cowden syndrome, a genetic disorder characterized by multiple benign tumors and an increased risk of certain cancers. Mutations in the PTEN gene are identified in approximately 80% of cases involving germline mutations associated with Cowden syndrome. This highlights the importance of PTEN in both the diagnosis and understanding of this syndrome."}{"title": "PACINI ET AL.:Pacini et al. is a reference cited in the context of the frequency of familial cases of medullary thyroid carcinoma."}{"title": "MEDULLARY THYROID CARCINOMA:Medullary thyroid carcinoma is a specific type of thyroid cancer that originates from the parafollicular C cells of the thyroid gland. This cancer is notable for its association with elevated levels of calcitonin, which can be used for diagnosis and monitoring of the disease. Medullary thyroid carcinoma is also linked to certain genetic syndromes, including Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia type 2B (MEN2B) and Cowden syndrome. The disease has the potential to metastasize, making careful monitoring and treatment essential. It is the subject of various studies and clinical trials aimed at improving understanding and management of the condition. At the time of diagnosis, patients may already present with metastases, highlighting the aggressive nature of this cancer."}{"title": "GUIDELINES TASK FORCE ON THYROID NODULES AND DIFFERENTIATED THYROID CANCER:This task force is part of the American Thyroid Association and is responsible for developing management guidelines for thyroid conditions."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE COWDEN:El s\u00edndrome de Cowden es un s\u00edndrome raro de tumores asociado a mutaciones en el gen PTEN. Se caracteriza por la formaci\u00f3n de hamartomas en m\u00faltiples tejidos y un riesgo aumentado de desarrollar varios tipos de c\u00e1ncer. Entre los tipos de neoplasias m\u00e1s comunes asociadas con este s\u00edndrome se encuentran el c\u00e1ncer de mama, tiroides y endometrio. Adem\u00e1s, el s\u00edndrome puede provocar un crecimiento hamartomatoso en tejidos como el colon y la piel."}{"title": "TIROIDECTOM\u00cdA:Tiroidectom\u00eda is a surgical procedure that involves the removal of all or part of the thyroid gland. It is particularly recommended for patients diagnosed with medullary thyroid carcinoma, especially in cases where specific mutations, such as those associated with MEN2B, are present. This procedure can have implications for parathyroid hormone levels, potentially affecting the patient's overall hormonal balance."}{"title": "LINFADENECTOM\u00cdA CERVICAL:La linfadenectom\u00eda cervical es un procedimiento que se debe realizar junto con la tiroidectom\u00eda total en el tratamiento del carcinoma medular de tiroides."}{"title": "M918T MEN2B:La mutaci\u00f3n M918T MEN2B es una mutaci\u00f3n gen\u00e9tica asociada con un alto riesgo de carcinoma medular de tiroides y requiere cirug\u00eda profil\u00e1ctica antes del primer a\u00f1o de vida."}{"title": "GU\u00cdA DE CARCINOMA MEDULAR DE TIROIDES DE LA ATA:La Gu\u00eda de carcinoma medular de tiroides de la ATA proporciona recomendaciones sobre el manejo y tratamiento de las mutaciones que pueden causar carcinoma medular de tiroides."}{"title": "HAMPARTOMAS:Los hamartomas son crecimientos benignos que pueden presentarse en pacientes con s\u00edndrome de Cowden, afectando tejidos como colon y piel."}{"title": "CALCITONINA:Calcitonin, or \"calcitonina\" in Spanish, is a hormone produced by the C cells of the thyroid gland. It plays a significant role in regulating calcium levels in the body by inhibiting osteoclastic bone resorption, which helps to decrease bone loss. Calcitonin is utilized in the treatment of conditions such as osteoporosis, although its effectiveness in reducing fractures remains a topic of debate. Additionally, it is employed in managing severe hypercalcemia.\n\nThe hormone is also important in the context of medullary thyroid carcinoma, particularly in patients with potential RET mutations. In these cases, calcitonin levels are monitored to assess the risk of developing this type of cancer, as well as to evaluate the progression of the disease and the necessity for surgical intervention. Overall, calcitonin serves both therapeutic and diagnostic purposes in various medical contexts."}{"title": "HIPOPARATIROIDISMO:HIPOPARATIROIDISMO, or hypoparathyroidism, is a medical condition characterized by insufficient production of parathyroid hormone, which results in low levels of calcium in the blood. This condition can arise as a complication following total thyroidectomy and should be considered in surgical management. Additionally, hypoparathyroidism can lead to various complications, including hypomagnesemia and osteoporosis, due to its impact on calcium and phosphate metabolism. The condition may occur due to several factors, including the treatment of thyroid disease and infiltrative diseases that affect the parathyroid glands."}{"title": "CARCINOMA MEDULAR DE TIROIDES:"}{"title": "MEDULLARY THYROID CANCER:Medullary thyroid cancer is a type of thyroid cancer that can be hereditary and is associated with multiple endocrine neoplasia syndromes."}{"title": "MEN2:MEN2, or Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia type 2, is a genetic syndrome characterized by a clear association with specific activating mutations in the RET proto-oncogene. This condition is inherited in an autosomal dominant manner and has significant implications for the diagnosis and treatment of associated tumors. MEN2 primarily increases the risk of developing medullary thyroid carcinoma and pheochromocytoma, distinguishing it from MEN1, which involves different types of tumors. The syndrome is considered rare and is marked by the onset and aggressiveness of medullary thyroid carcinoma, along with the potential for other endocrine tumors."}{"title": "RET ONCOGENE:The RET oncogene is a gene that, when mutated, is associated with multiple endocrine neoplasia type 2 and medullary thyroid carcinoma."}{"title": "CHAMBON G:Chambon G is an author of a study related to the measurement of serum thyrocalcitonin in patients with thyroid disorders."}{"title": "COSTANTE G:Costante G is an author of a study that discusses the predictive value of serum calcitonin levels for diagnosing medullary thyroid carcinoma."}{"title": "BIOMARKER-BASED RISK STRATIFICATION:Biomarker-based risk stratification is a method used to assess the risk of medullary thyroid cancer in patients based on specific biomarkers."}{"title": "ANNALS OF SURGERY:The \"ANNALS OF SURGERY\" is a peer-reviewed medical journal that focuses on publishing research related to surgical practices and outcomes. It features a variety of articles, including meta-analyses concerning immunonutrition in surgery and studies that estimate mortality risk in preoperative patients. Additionally, the journal includes research on specific surgical conditions, such as medullary thyroid cancer. Through its comprehensive coverage of surgical topics, the \"ANNALS OF SURGERY\" serves as a significant resource for medical professionals in the field of surgery."}{"title": "JOURNAL OF CLINICAL ENDOCRINOLOGY AND METABOLISM:The Journal of Clinical Endocrinology and Metabolism is a prominent medical journal dedicated to publishing research on various aspects of endocrinology and metabolism. It covers a wide range of topics, including the impacts of diet on health, endocrine disorders such as medullary thyroid carcinoma, and hormonal and metabolic disorders. The journal features studies on vitamin D deficiency in cystic fibrosis patients, as well as research related to anorexia nervosa and its treatments. Through its diverse array of publications, the Journal of Clinical Endocrinology and Metabolism contributes significantly to the understanding and advancement of knowledge in the fields of endocrinology and metabolism."}{"title": "CLINICAL ONCOLOGY:Clinical Oncology is a journal that publishes research and reviews on cancer treatment and management, including studies on medullary thyroid carcinoma."}{"title": "SURGICAL CURABILITY:"}{"title": "MEN2A:MEN2A, or Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia Type 2A, is a genetic condition characterized by mutations in the RET proto-oncogene. This autosomal dominant disorder is primarily associated with a high risk of developing specific tumors, including medullary thyroid carcinoma (MTC), which occurs in 100% of patients, bilateral pheochromocytomas in approximately 50% of cases, and hyperparathyroidism in 20-30% of individuals. The syndrome necessitates early preventive treatment due to its association with these malignancies, particularly medullary thyroid carcinoma and pheochromocytoma. Overall, MEN2A is a significant health concern that requires careful monitoring and management to mitigate the risks of these endocrine tumors."}{"title": "ATA:The American Thyroid Association (ATA) is an organization dedicated to providing comprehensive guidelines and recommendations for the management of thyroid diseases. Among its key contributions, the ATA offers specific guidance for the diagnosis and management of medullary thyroid carcinoma, including risk stratification associated with various genetic mutations. The ATA's resources are essential for healthcare professionals in effectively addressing thyroid-related conditions and ensuring optimal patient care."}{"title": "NANETS:The North American Neuroendocrine Tumor Society (NANETS) is an organization dedicated to the diagnosis, study, and management of neuroendocrine tumors in North America. It aims to enhance the understanding and treatment of these tumors, providing resources and support for both healthcare professionals and patients affected by this condition."}{"title": "SIPPEL RS:Sippel RS is a researcher involved in the North American Neuroendocrine Tumor Society guidelines."}{"title": "O'DORISIO MS:O'Dorisio MS is a researcher who contributed to the NANETS guidelines for neuroendocrine tumors."}{"title": "VINIK AI:Vinik AI is a researcher who contributed to the NANETS guidelines for neuroendocrine tumors."}{"title": "PACAK K:Pacak K is a researcher who contributed to the NANETS guidelines for neuroendocrine tumors."}{"title": "MULLIGAN LM:Mulligan LM is a researcher who studied point mutations in the RET proto-oncogene related to MEN2B."}{"title": "MARX SJ:Marx SJ is a researcher who has written about multiple endocrine neoplasia."}{"title": "WELLS SA:WELLS SA is a prominent researcher and author in the field of thyroid cancer, specifically focusing on medullary thyroid carcinoma. They have been actively involved in developing guidelines and conducting studies related to this type of cancer. WELLS SA's contributions include significant input into the management guidelines for medullary thyroid carcinoma, highlighting their expertise and commitment to advancing knowledge in this area."}{"title": "CARCINOMA MEDULAR:Carcinoma medular is a type of thyroid cancer that is associated with mutations in the RET proto-oncogene. It is often diagnosed in patients with Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia types 2A (MEN2A) and 2B (MEN2B). This form of cancer can secrete hormones, leading to symptoms such as diarrhea and flushing."}{"title": "TIROGLOBULINA:Tiroglobulina is a protein used as a tumor marker in the follow-up of patients with differentiated thyroid cancer."}{"title": "PET 18F-FDG:PET 18F-FDG is a type of positron emission tomography (PET) that is utilized primarily for staging and evaluating treatment responses in patients with thyroid cancer. It plays a significant role in the diagnosis and management of various cancers, particularly differentiated thyroid cancer. PET 18F-FDG detects metabolic activity in tumors, providing valuable insights into cancer progression and treatment efficacy. However, it is important to note that this imaging method has low sensitivity for detecting medullary thyroid carcinoma, which may limit its effectiveness in certain cases."}{"title": "I-131:I-131 is a radioactive isotope used in the treatment of thyroid cancer."}{"title": "LEBOULLEUX S:Leboulleux S is a researcher involved in studies related to differentiated thyroid cancer."}{"title": "TBG:TBG (thyroxine-binding globulin) is a protein that transports thyroid hormones in the bloodstream and is influenced by various factors including estrogen levels."}{"title": "DIFFERENTIATED THYROID CANCER:Differentiated thyroid cancer is a type of thyroid cancer that arises from follicular or parafollicular cells and is typically treated with I-131."}{"title": "AMERICAN JOINT COMMITTEE ON CANCER:The American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) is an organization that provides guidelines for cancer staging, including the TNM classification system."}{"title": "AJCC CANCER STAGING MANUAL:The AJCC Cancer Staging Manual is a publication that outlines the classification and staging of various cancers, including thyroid cancer."}{"title": "RISK OF RECURRENCE:The risk of recurrence refers to the likelihood that the thyroid cancer will return after treatment, as assessed by the ATA guidelines."}{"title": "HISTOLOGY:Histology refers to the microscopic examination of the tumor's cells, which is crucial for determining the aggressiveness of the cancer."}{"title": "METASTASIS:Metastasis is the spread of cancer cells from the original tumor site in the thyroid to other parts of the body, which affects staging and treatment decisions."}{"title": "CALCITONIN:Calcitonin is a hormone produced by the thyroid gland that plays a crucial role in regulating calcium levels in the blood. It is particularly significant in the context of medullary thyroid carcinoma, where it serves as a tumor marker. Calcitonin's levels are monitored post-surgery to predict the evolution of patients with this type of cancer, and it is also used to assess the presence and extent of the disease. Additionally, calcitonin is utilized as a biomarker in the diagnosis and management of medullary thyroid cancer, highlighting its importance in both clinical and diagnostic settings."}{"title": "MACHENS A:Machens A is a researcher known for their contributions to studies focused on biomarker-based risk stratification for medullary thyroid cancer."}{"title": "DRALLE H:Dralle H is a prominent contributor to the European Society of Endocrinology guidelines, specifically focusing on the management of adrenal incidentalomas. With a specialization in endocrine surgery, Dralle H plays a significant role in shaping the guidelines that govern the clinical approach to these conditions. Additionally, Dralle H is actively involved in research related to medullary thyroid carcinoma, contributing to the development of management guidelines and engaging in studies that explore biomarker-based risk stratification for this type of cancer. Through these efforts, Dralle H has established a comprehensive expertise in both adrenal incidentalomas and medullary thyroid carcinoma, making valuable contributions to the field of endocrinology."}{"title": "TIROIDECTOM\u00cdA TOTAL:Tiroidectom\u00eda total, or total thyroidectomy, is a surgical procedure indicated for patients with specific RET mutations to prevent the development of medullary thyroid carcinoma. Additionally, it is recommended for patients diagnosed with thyroid cancer, as outlined in medical guidelines. This procedure involves the complete removal of the thyroid gland and is a critical intervention for managing certain thyroid-related conditions."}{"title": "VACIAMIENTO DE COMPARTIMENTO VI:Compartment VI dissection is a surgical procedure that may be indicated in the management of thyroid cancer, particularly when lymph nodes are involved."}{"title": "VACIAMIENTO GANGLIONAR:Lymphadenectomy is a surgical procedure to remove lymph nodes that may be affected by cancer, as indicated in the management of thyroid cancer."}{"title": "NIVELES DE CALCITONINA:Calcitonin levels are measured to assess the risk of metastasis in patients with medullary thyroid cancer."}{"title": "ELISEI R:Elisei R is a researcher who co-authored the guidelines for the management of medullary thyroid carcinoma."}{"title": "EVAN DB:Evan DB is a researcher who contributed to the American Thyroid Association guidelines on medullary thyroid carcinoma."}{"title": "GAGEL RF:Gagel RF is a researcher involved in the study and management of medullary thyroid carcinoma."}{"title": "TOLEDO SPA:Toledo SPA is a researcher who studied hypercalcitonemia and its implications in medullary thyroid carcinoma."}{"title": "GIRAUDET ET AL.:Giraudet et al. conducted a study on imaging medullary thyroid carcinoma with elevated calcitonin levels, providing insights into the sensitivity of various imaging techniques."}{"title": "SALTIKI ET AL.:Saltiki et al. conducted a series of studies on the diagnosis and evolution of medullary thyroid carcinoma, comparing familial and sporadic cases."}{"title": "CERVICAL ULTRASOUND:Cervical ultrasound is a diagnostic imaging technique that plays a crucial role in the management of patients diagnosed with medullary thyroid carcinoma. It is recommended for all such patients to assess for lymph node metastases, providing essential information for treatment planning. Additionally, cervical ultrasound serves as a key imaging method to evaluate the outcomes of surgical interventions in these patients, helping to monitor their post-operative status and detect any potential complications or recurrences."}{"title": "MRI:Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI) is a sophisticated medical imaging technique that provides detailed visualization of internal structures within the body. It is particularly effective in identifying tumors and assessing various conditions, including the evaluation of hepatic iron stores. Additionally, MRI plays a crucial role in detecting bone metastases, especially in patients diagnosed with medullary thyroid carcinoma. This versatility makes MRI an invaluable tool in modern medical diagnostics."}{"title": "BONE SCINTIGRAPHY:Bone scintigraphy is an imaging technique used to detect bone metastases in patients with medullary thyroid carcinoma."}{"title": "NIVEL DE CALCITONINA:Niveles de calcitonina are used as a biomarker to assess the presence and extent of medullary thyroid carcinoma, with higher levels indicating more advanced disease."}{"title": "GAMMAGRAF\u00cdA \u00d3SEA:Gammagraf\u00eda \u00f3sea is an imaging technique used to assess bone metastases in patients diagnosed with medullary thyroid carcinoma."}{"title": "CANCER MEDULAR DE TIROIDES:CANCER MEDULAR DE TIROIDES, also known as medullary thyroid carcinoma (CMT), is a type of cancer that can arise in patients who have mutations in the RET proto-oncogene. This condition is particularly associated with multiple endocrine neoplasia type 2 (MEN2)."}{"title": "PROTOONCOG\u00c9N RET:El protooncog\u00e9n RET es un gen que, cuando presenta mutaciones, puede dar origen a carcinomas medulares familiares."}{"title": "ANT\u00cdGENO CARCINOEMBRIONARIO:El ant\u00edgeno carcinoembrionario (CEA) es un marcador que se utiliza para monitorear la evoluci\u00f3n del carcinoma medular de tiroides."}{"title": "ADENOPAT\u00cdAS PATOL\u00d3GICAS:"}{"title": "PELLEGRITI ET AL.:Pellegriti et al. conducted a study evaluating the outcomes of 63 patients operated on for medullary thyroid carcinoma."}{"title": "BARBET ET AL.:Barbet et al. conducted a study assessing the prognostic impact of calcitonin doubling times in patients with medullary thyroid carcinoma."}{"title": "VANDETANIB:Vandetanib is a tyrosine kinase inhibitor used in the treatment of advanced medullary thyroid carcinoma."}{"title": "CABOZANTINIB:Cabozantinib is a tyrosine kinase inhibitor that has shown benefits in patients with progressive medullary thyroid carcinoma."}{"title": "CARCINOEMBRYONIC ANTIGEN:Carcinoembryonic antigen (CEA) is a tumor marker utilized in the medical field, particularly in the assessment of various cancers, including medullary thyroid carcinoma. It is often used in conjunction with calcitonin to evaluate the prognosis of patients diagnosed with this specific type of cancer. CEA serves as an important indicator in monitoring disease progression and treatment response in affected individuals."}{"title": "63 PACIENTES:The study evaluated 63 patients who underwent surgery for medullary thyroid carcinoma, providing data on their outcomes."}{"title": "BRITISH JOURNAL OF CANCER:The British Journal of Cancer is a peer-reviewed medical journal dedicated to publishing research on various aspects of cancer. It encompasses a wide range of topics, including clinical studies, meta-analyses, treatment, prevention, and epidemiology. Notably, the journal also features studies focused on specific types of cancer, such as medullary thyroid carcinoma outcomes. Through its comprehensive coverage, the British Journal of Cancer serves as a significant resource for researchers and healthcare professionals in the field of oncology."}{"title": "VANDATENIB:A drug used in clinical trials for treating locally advanced or metastatic medullary thyroid cancer, as part of a randomized, double-blind phase III trial."}{"title": "ORTIGA-CARVALHO TM:A researcher who has studied thyroid hormone receptors and resistance to thyroid hormone disorders."}{"title": "PHASE III TRIAL:A clinical trial phase that tests the effectiveness of a treatment in a larger group of patients, such as the trial involving Vandetanib for medullary thyroid cancer."}{"title": "HYPERTIROXINEMIA:A condition characterized by elevated levels of thyroxine in the blood, which can occur during pregnancy or due to other thyroid disorders."}{"title": "RESISTANCE TO HORMONES:A condition where the body's tissues do not respond properly to thyroid hormones, which can complicate diagnosis and treatment."}{"title": "SOCIN:Socin is an organization that conducted a series of studies on TSHomas, focusing on the positivity rates of \u03b1 subunit elevation in pituitary tumors."}{"title": "ALFONSO JOS\u00c9 VIDAL CASARIEGO:Alfonso Jos\u00e9 Vidal Casariego is a specialist in Endocrinology and Nutrition, with a Doctorate in Medicine from the University of A Coru\u00f1a and currently working at the Complexo Hospitalario Universitario de A Coru\u00f1a."}{"title": "A CORU\u00d1A:A Coru\u00f1a is a city in Spain where the Complexo Hospitalario Universitario is located, and where Alfonso Jos\u00e9 Vidal Casariego practices medicine."}{"title": "WEMEAU J.-L:Wemeau J.-L is a co-author of the European Thyroid Association Guidelines for the Diagnosis and Treatment of Thyrotropin-Secreting Pituitary Tumors, contributing to the field of endocrinology."}{"title": "SACYL:SACYL is the health service of the Castilla y Le\u00f3n region in Spain, dedicated to funding various health projects, including those related to endocrinology. The organization supports a range of research initiatives in the field of health and medicine, with notable projects led by individuals such as Ana M.\u00aa Urioste Fondo. Through its funding efforts, SACYL plays a significant role in advancing health research and improving medical outcomes in the region."}{"title": "UNIVERSIDAD DE A CORU\u00d1A:The University of A Coru\u00f1a is an educational institution where various academic programs are offered, including a Master's in Research Methodology."}{"title": "ANA M.\u00aa URIOSTE FONDO:Ana M.\u00aa Urioste Fondo is a specialist in Endocrinology and Nutrition, currently working at the Complexo Hospitalario Universitario de A Coru\u00f1a."}{"title": "UNIDAD DE NUTRICI\u00d3N CL\u00cdNICA DEL COMPLEJO ASISTENCIAL UNIVERSITARIO DE LE\u00d3N:The Clinical Nutrition Unit at the Complejo Asistencial Universitario de Le\u00f3n (CAULE) is a medical department focused on nutrition-related healthcare."}{"title": "SOCIEDAD CASTELLANO-LEONESA DE ENDOCRINOLOG\u00cdA, DIABETES Y NUTRICI\u00d3N:The Castilian-Leonese Society of Endocrinology, Diabetes, and Nutrition is a professional organization where medical professionals engage in education and research in the field of nutrition and endocrinology."}{"title": "HARMONY OUTCOMES:The HARMONY OUTCOMES study is a clinical trial in which Ana M.\u00aa Urioste Fondo has participated, focusing on health outcomes related to endocrinology."}{"title": "INSUPAR:INSUPAR is another clinical trial in which Ana M.\u00aa Urioste Fondo has been involved, contributing to research in clinical nutrition."}{"title": "COMPLEXO ASISTENCIAL UNIVERSITARIO DE LE\u00d3N:"}{"title": "MAASTRICHT INDEX:The Maastricht Index is a prognostic index used to assess nutritional status, characterized by the use of various nutritional risk markers."}{"title": "BIA MULTIFRECUENCIA:Multifrequency bioelectrical impedance analysis (BIA) is a method used to estimate body water and composition in individuals, particularly useful in clinical settings."}{"title": "LINFOCITOS TOTALES:Total lymphocytes are a type of white blood cell used as a marker in nutritional assessments."}{"title": "GALICIA:Galicia is an autonomous community in Spain known for its unique cultural identity and geographical features. In recent years, it has become a focal point for studies on nutritional risk assessments in hospitalized patients, highlighting the region's commitment to healthcare and patient well-being. Additionally, Galicia has established its own catalog of enteral formulas, which restricts the number of formulas approved for funding, ensuring that only certain products are available for patients in need of nutritional support. To continue treatment for nutritional needs, patients in Galicia are required to submit a justification report to the General Subdirectorate of Pharmacy and Health Products, reflecting the region's structured approach to healthcare management. Furthermore, Galicia faces significant challenges with obesity prevalence rates, underscoring the importance of ongoing research and intervention in nutritional health within the community."}{"title": "EDEMATOSO:Edematous states refer to conditions where excess fluid accumulates in the body's tissues, which can affect nutritional status and body composition."}{"title": "MASA LIBRE DE GRASA:Lean body mass refers to the weight of everything in the body except fat, an important measure in assessing body composition."}{"title": "OBESIDAD M\u00d3RBIDA:\"OBESIDAD M\u00d3RBIDA,\" or morbid obesity, is a severe medical condition characterized by excessive body weight that significantly increases the risk of various health complications. This condition has been discussed in clinical cases, highlighting its impact on patients who often experience multiple attempts at weight loss and may ultimately require surgical intervention, such as bariatric surgery. Morbid obesity is resistant to conventional treatment methods and is associated with serious health issues, including diabetes and an increased risk of pancreatic cancer. Management of morbid obesity often necessitates specific nutritional strategies, particularly for critically ill patients, to address the complex health challenges it presents. Overall, morbid obesity is a critical health concern that demands comprehensive medical attention and intervention."}{"title": "RUIZ L\u00d3PEZ:Ruiz L\u00f3pez is a medical doctor who contributed to the work on nutrition in older adults."}{"title": "ARTACHO MART\u00cdN LAGOS:Artacho Mart\u00edn Lagos is a researcher involved in the study of nutrition in older adults."}{"title": "QUILES MORALES:Quiles Morales is a researcher who co-authored the work on nutrition in older adults."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N EN EL ADULTO MAYOR:A chapter in a book discussing nutrition specifically for older adults."}{"title": "LATHAM:Latham is a researcher who authored works on human nutrition in developing countries, contributing to the understanding of malnutrition."}{"title": "ALIMENTACI\u00d3N Y NUTRICI\u00d3N:A collection by FAO that discusses food and nutrition, focusing on global issues related to hunger and malnutrition."}{"title": "GONZALO MAR\u00cdN M:Gonzalo Mar\u00edn M is an author who has contributed to research in clinical nutrition and metabolism. He has also collaborated on works related to nutritional requirements and diet therapy. His contributions reflect a focus on understanding the complexities of nutrition and its application in clinical settings."}{"title": "DIETOTERAPIA, NUTRICI\u00d3N CL\u00cdNICA Y METABOLISMO:\"DIETOTERAPIA, NUTRICI\u00d3N CL\u00cdNICA Y METABOLISMO\" is a comprehensive medical text that explores the intricate relationship between diet therapy, clinical nutrition, and metabolism. This publication delves into various aspects of nutritional practices, including parenteral nutrition, and emphasizes the importance of dietary controls and their implications for health. It provides valuable insights into nutritional guidelines and practices, as well as the interactions between drugs and diet. Edited by multiple authors, including Olveira Fuster G., this work serves as an essential resource for healthcare professionals seeking to understand the role of nutrition in patient care and the impact of dietary interventions on health outcomes."}{"title": "RECOMENDACIONES DIET\u00c9TICAS:The entity \"RECOMENDACIONES DIET\u00c9TICAS\" refers to dietary recommendations, which are guidelines established to ensure that individuals receive the appropriate amount of nutrients and energy in their diet. These recommendations are particularly important for children, as they help to guide nutrient intake during critical growth periods. Additionally, dietary recommendations are essential for patients with chronic kidney disease, as they provide specific guidelines to maintain nutritional status and overall health. Overall, these dietary guidelines serve to promote well-being and prevent nutritional deficiencies across different populations."}{"title": "IRETON-JONES:Ireton-Jones is a researcher focused on nutritional support for cancer patients. In addition to their research, Ireton-Jones is known for developing the Ireton-Jones equation, which is utilized to estimate energy expenditure in patients, particularly those with specific medical conditions. This equation serves as a valuable tool for calculating the energy needs of critically ill patients, highlighting its importance in clinical settings."}{"title": "GASTO EN REPOSO:El gasto energ\u00e9tico en reposo (GER) es la cantidad de energ\u00eda que el cuerpo utiliza en estado de reposo para mantener funciones vitales."}{"title": "GASTO ENERGETICO TOTAL:El gasto energ\u00e9tico total (GET) es la suma de todas las energ\u00edas gastadas por un individuo en un d\u00eda, incluyendo el gasto en reposo, la actividad f\u00edsica y la termog\u00e9nesis inducida por alimentos."}{"title": "TERMOG\u00c9NESIS INDUCIDA POR ALIMENTOS:La termog\u00e9nesis inducida por alimentos es la energ\u00eda utilizada por el cuerpo para digerir, absorber y metabolizar los alimentos consumidos."}{"title": "MASA MAGRA CORPORAL:La masa magra corporal se refiere a la parte del cuerpo que no es grasa, incluyendo m\u00fasculos, huesos y \u00f3rganos, y es un factor importante en el c\u00e1lculo del gasto energ\u00e9tico."}{"title": "FUNDACI\u00d3N SEEN:La Fundaci\u00f3n SEEN es una organizaci\u00f3n que se dedica a la investigaci\u00f3n y promoci\u00f3n de la salud endocrina en Espa\u00f1a, incluyendo el estudio de trastornos por d\u00e9ficit de yodo."}{"title": "GRUPO DE TRABAJO DE TRASTORNOS POR D\u00c9FICIT DE YODO:Este grupo de trabajo est\u00e1 compuesto por expertos que analizan y proponen soluciones para los problemas relacionados con el d\u00e9ficit de yodo en la poblaci\u00f3n."}{"title": "D\u00cdA DE LA SALUD:Un evento que se celebra para concienciar sobre la importancia de la salud y la nutrici\u00f3n, promoviendo h\u00e1bitos saludables."}{"title": "OLVEIRA FUSTER G:Olveira Fuster G is a notable author and editor recognized for significant contributions to the field of nutrition and diet therapy. He has authored an update on probiotics, prebiotics, and symbiotics in clinical nutrition, showcasing his expertise in these areas. Additionally, he has contributed to a manual that addresses nutritional needs across different life stages, further emphasizing his commitment to advancing knowledge in nutrition. Olveira Fuster G also serves as an editor and contributor to the book titled \"Dietoterapia, nutrici\u00f3n cl\u00ednica y metabolismo,\" which reflects his comprehensive understanding of clinical nutrition and metabolism. Through these works, Olveira Fuster G has established himself as a key figure in the literature surrounding nutritional requirements and diet therapy."}{"title": "DIETA EQUILIBRADA:\"DIETA EQUILIBRADA\" refers to a balanced diet that is crucial for maintaining overall health and preventing chronic diseases. It encompasses a variety of foods consumed in appropriate proportions, which is essential not only for general well-being but also for specific health management, such as preventing kidney stones. A balanced diet provides all the necessary nutrients required for optimal health and serves as a foundational aspect of nutritional education, highlighting its importance in disease prevention and health maintenance."}{"title": "FIBRA DIET\u00c9TICA:FIBRA DIET\u00c9TICA refers to dietary fiber, a crucial component of nutrition that plays a significant role in promoting digestive health. It is found in various food sources, including whole grains, legumes, vegetables, and fruits. Dietary fiber aids in digestion, helps stabilize blood sugar levels, and contributes to the reduction of energy density in foods, which can promote feelings of fullness and assist in weight control.\n\nResearch indicates that dietary fiber is particularly beneficial for the elderly, as it is linked to improved overall health. Additionally, it is essential for children's diets, supporting their digestive health. As a type of carbohydrate that the body cannot digest, dietary fiber is important for gut health and is associated with various health benefits, including the potential to inhibit the absorption of adenine, which may lower uric acid levels.\n\nFIBRA DIET\u00c9TICA is recognized in dietary recommendations and guidelines, such as those from the World Health Organization (WHO), emphasizing its importance in maintaining a balanced and healthy diet."}{"title": "RECOMENDACIONES DE INGESTA:Las recomendaciones de ingesta son pautas establecidas por organizaciones de salud para asegurar una nutrici\u00f3n adecuada en la poblaci\u00f3n."}{"title": "TRASTORNOS POR D\u00c9FICIT DE YODO:Los trastornos por d\u00e9ficit de yodo son condiciones de salud que resultan de una ingesta insuficiente de yodo, afectando la funci\u00f3n tiroidea."}{"title": "FEDERACI\u00d3N ESPA\u00d1OLA DE SOCIEDADES DE ALIMENTACI\u00d3N, NUTRICI\u00d3N Y DIET\u00c9TICA:The Federaci\u00f3n Espa\u00f1ola de Sociedades de Alimentaci\u00f3n, Nutrici\u00f3n y Diet\u00e9tica (FESNAD) is an organization that provides consensus on dietary fats and oils for the adult Spanish population."}{"title": "INSTITUTE OF MEDICINE:The Institute of Medicine (IOM) is a nonprofit organization that operates as part of the National Academy of Sciences. It is dedicated to providing expert advice on health and medicine to decision-makers and the public. The IOM offers a wide range of services, including the development of clinical guidelines, nutritional guidelines, and dietary reference intakes for various nutrients. It focuses on delivering evidence-based information regarding health and nutrition, which encompasses dietary recommendations and requirements. Additionally, the IOM defines adequate fiber intake during pregnancy and lactation, ensuring that its health recommendations and guidelines are grounded in scientific evidence. Overall, the Institute of Medicine plays a crucial role in shaping health policy and providing comprehensive health recommendations, including those related to dietary intake."}{"title": "LUENGO P\u00c9REZ LM:Luengo P\u00e9rez LM is an author who contributed to the manual on nutrition in different life stages."}{"title": "BEATO V\u00cdBORA P:Beato V\u00edbora P is an author who contributed to the manual on nutrition in different life stages."}{"title": "NICOL\u00c1S BLANCO M:Nicol\u00e1s Blanco M is an author who contributed to the manual on nutrition in different life stages."}{"title": "METABOLISMO:Metabolismo encompasses all biochemical processes that occur within living organisms to maintain life, including essential functions such as digestion, nutrient absorption, and the conversion of food into energy. It is closely related to nutrition and exercise, playing a crucial role in understanding the nutritional needs of individuals, particularly during specific conditions such as pregnancy, obesity, and recovery from burns or severe trauma. The metabolic processes are vital for sustaining life and can be influenced by various medical conditions, affecting how the body utilizes energy derived from food. Overall, metabolismo is integral to the health and well-being of living organisms, highlighting the importance of proper nutrition and metabolic function."}{"title": "DIETOTERAPIA:Dietoterapia is a comprehensive therapeutic approach that focuses on diet management and clinical nutrition to treat various health conditions. It is particularly significant for patients recovering from digestive surgeries, as it emphasizes tailored dietary recommendations to optimize recovery. The practice encompasses clinical nutrition and metabolism, aiming to manage dietary needs through specific food choices and meal planning.\n\nDietoterapia plays a crucial role in the early stages of conditions such as amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (ALS), where dietary modifications are essential to enhance intake and reduce dysphagia. It also addresses the nutritional requirements of patients with chronic diseases, including cystic fibrosis and metabolic disorders, by implementing controlled diets that cater to specific health issues like diabetes and obesity.\n\nThe organization behind Dietoterapia is involved in the publication of relevant literature and the development of nutrition products, highlighting its commitment to advancing clinical nutrition practices. This approach includes dietary therapy for managing inflammatory bowel disease, pancreatic diseases, and other health conditions, with a focus on improving overall health and nutritional status.\n\nDietoterapia also encompasses the use of diet in the treatment of diseases, including cancer prevention and management, and considers the impact of dietary factors such as sugar intake on weight and dental health. It is a vital aspect of nutrition and health, particularly in clinical settings where patients may require specialized dietary interventions, including parenteral nutrition in certain scenarios.\n\nOverall, Dietoterapia represents a holistic approach to dietary therapy, emphasizing the importance of nutrition in managing health conditions and improving patient outcomes."}{"title": "GINEBRA:Ginebra es una ciudad en Suiza, sede de la Organizaci\u00f3n Mundial de la Salud, donde se realizan importantes reuniones sobre salud global."}{"title": "JA HURTADO SUAZO:JA Hurtado Suazo es un autor que ha contribuido a la literatura sobre nutrici\u00f3n durante la gestaci\u00f3n y lactancia."}{"title": "MA KOMINIAREK:MA Kominiarek es un autor que ha escrito sobre recomendaciones nutricionales en el embarazo y la lactancia."}{"title": "M:M es un autor que ha investigado sobre la nutrici\u00f3n y el yodo durante el embarazo y la lactancia."}{"title": "YODURO POT\u00c1SICO:El yoduro pot\u00e1sico es un suplemento de yodo recomendado durante la gestaci\u00f3n para asegurar un adecuado nivel de yodo en la madre y el feto."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N DURANTE LA GESTACI\u00d3N:La nutrici\u00f3n durante la gestaci\u00f3n se refiere a las recomendaciones y pr\u00e1cticas alimenticias que deben seguir las mujeres embarazadas para asegurar la salud del feto."}{"title": "F\u00c1RMACOS ANTICONVULSIVOS:"}{"title": "INGESTAS DIET\u00c9TICAS DE REFERENCIA:Ingestas Diet\u00e9ticas de Referencia (IDR) are dietary reference intakes specifically developed for Spain and published in 2010. These guidelines serve as a framework for dietary recommendations aimed at the Spanish population, providing essential information on the intake of various nutrients. Among the nutrients addressed in the IDR are vitamin D and calcium, highlighting the importance of these elements in the diet. Overall, the IDR represents a comprehensive approach to ensuring adequate nutrition and health for individuals in Spain."}{"title": "CU\u00c9LLAR OLMEDO LA:Cu\u00e9llar Olmedo LA is an author recognized for contributions to the literature on enteral nutrition, particularly focusing on its administration methods. Their work is referenced in discussions surrounding the practices and guidelines related to enteral nutrition, highlighting their significance in this field."}{"title": "TERROBA LARUMBE C:Terroba Larumbe C is an author who contributed to the literature on enteral nutrition."}{"title": "CORDERO VAQUERO AA:Cordero Vaquero AA is an author recognized for contributions to the literature on enteral nutrition, particularly focusing on its administration methods. Their work is referenced in discussions surrounding the practices and techniques involved in enteral nutrition, highlighting their significance in this field."}{"title": "DE LUIS ROM\u00c1N DA:De Luis Rom\u00e1n DA is an author recognized for his contributions to the field of nutrition, specifically in the areas of enteral and parenteral nutrition. He has been referenced in discussions regarding the administration methods of enteral nutrition, highlighting his expertise in this area. Additionally, De Luis Rom\u00e1n DA has addressed the complications associated with parenteral nutrition, further demonstrating his comprehensive understanding of nutritional practices. His work has significantly contributed to the literature on enteral nutrition, establishing him as a notable figure in this domain."}{"title": "MUTUAL NUTRITION:The event of mutual nutrition refers to the process of providing nutritional support to patients who cannot meet their caloric needs orally, particularly in post-operative settings."}{"title": "HEAD AND NECK SURGERY:Head and neck surgery refers to surgical procedures performed on the head and neck region, often requiring nutritional support due to the complexity and recovery involved."}{"title": "GASTROINTESTINAL SURGERY:Gastrointestinal surgery involves surgical procedures on the digestive tract, which may necessitate enteral nutrition for recovery and healing."}{"title": "WEIMANN A:Weimann A is a researcher and author who is associated with the ESPEN guidelines on clinical nutrition in surgery. He has contributed to the development of these guidelines, which are essential for providing evidence-based recommendations in the field of clinical nutrition for surgical patients."}{"title": "BRAGA M:Braga M is a prominent researcher and author known for significant contributions to the field of surgical nutrition. He has focused on enhanced recovery after surgery and the impact of immunonutrition on surgical outcomes. As an expert in this area, Braga M is associated with the ESPEN guidelines, specifically those pertaining to clinical nutrition in surgery and parenteral nutrition related to surgical practices. Additionally, he has played a vital role in formulating consensus recommendations from the North American Surgical Nutrition Summit, further establishing his influence and expertise in the field of surgical nutrition."}{"title": "CARLI F:Carli F is a prominent researcher and author recognized for her contributions to the field of clinical nutrition, particularly in the context of surgery. She is associated with the ESPEN guidelines on clinical nutrition, which provide essential recommendations for managing nutritional care in surgical patients. Additionally, Carli F is actively involved in researching perioperative care specifically for patients undergoing pancreaticoduodenectomy, a complex surgical procedure. Furthermore, she has contributed to the recommendations stemming from the North American Surgical Nutrition Summit, highlighting her commitment to advancing nutritional practices in surgical settings."}{"title": "HIGASHIGUCHI T:Higashiguchi T is a researcher and author associated with the ESPEN guidelines on clinical nutrition in surgery."}{"title": "H\u00dcBNER M:H\u00fcbner M is a researcher and author known for contributions to the field of clinical nutrition in surgery, particularly through involvement with the ESPEN guidelines. Additionally, H\u00fcbner M has conducted research focused on immunonutrition in gastrointestinal surgery, highlighting a commitment to advancing knowledge and practices in nutritional support for surgical patients."}{"title": "KLEK S:KLEK S is a prominent researcher focused on the field of immunonutrition and its implications for surgical patients. He has contributed significantly to the understanding of how immunonutrition affects malnourished individuals undergoing surgery. In addition to his research, KLEK S is one of the authors of the ESPEN guidelines, which provide comprehensive recommendations for the management of acute intestinal failure. His work is recognized within the clinical nutrition community, particularly in the context of surgery, where he has played a key role in shaping best practices through his involvement with the ESPEN guidelines on clinical nutrition."}{"title": "DIARREA GRAVE PERSISTENTE:Diarrea grave persistente is a serious condition that can affect nutritional status and is a contraindication for enteral nutrition."}{"title": "V\u00d3MITOS INCOERCIBLES:\"V\u00d3MITOS INCOERCIBLES\" refers to episodes of vomiting that are uncontrollable and cannot be managed effectively. These episodes can lead to significant health issues, including dehydration and complications that may arise from the inability to maintain proper nutrition. Specifically, v\u00f3mitos incoercibles can hinder the safe administration of enteral nutrition, making it challenging to provide adequate dietary support to affected individuals."}{"title": "F\u00cdSTULA ENTERICA DE ALTO D\u00c9BITO:F\u00edstula enterica de alto d\u00e9bito refers to a high-output enteric fistula that can complicate nutritional management and is a contraindication for enteral nutrition."}{"title": "MADRIGAL:Madrigal refers to multiple contexts, primarily associated with the capital city of Spain, Madrid, where a relevant manual was published. Additionally, Madrigal is a fictional character used in clinical nutrition discussions, representing a patient scenario that aids in understanding nutritional guidelines. Furthermore, Madrigal is also recognized as an author who has contributed to the analysis of quality indicators in nutritional support, highlighting the importance of effective nutritional practices in clinical settings."}{"title": "PANCREATITIS AGUDA GRAVE NECROSANTE:"}{"title": "TERRROBA LARUMBE C:Terrroba Larumbe C is an author referenced in the context of enteral nutrition and its administration methods."}{"title": "TOLEDO:Toledo is a city in Spain known for its rich history and cultural significance. It is home to the Aula M\u00e9dica, a medical publishing house that published a notable book on clinical nutrition. This book, which focuses on clinical nutrition and metabolism, has been referenced in various contexts, highlighting Toledo's role as a center for medical literature in this field."}{"title": "F\u00cdSTULAS DIGESTIVAS:Digestive fistulas are abnormal connections in the digestive tract that may require specific nutritional management."}{"title": "HERNIAS HIATALES:Hiatal hernias are conditions that can complicate the placement of gastrostomy tubes."}{"title": "V\u00d3LVULO G\u00c1STRICO:V\u00d3LVULO G\u00c1STRICO is a medical condition characterized by the twisting of the stomach on itself, which can result in obstruction. This condition necessitates careful consideration during medical procedures due to the potential complications it may cause. Additionally, gastric volvulus can contraindicate the placement of gastrostomy tubes, highlighting the importance of thorough evaluation and management in affected patients."}{"title": "HIPERTENSI\u00d3N PORTAL:HIPERTENSI\u00d3N PORTAL refers to a medical condition characterized by increased blood pressure in the portal venous system, which is often a complication associated with chronic liver diseases, particularly cirrhosis. This condition contributes to the retention of fluids in patients suffering from liver cirrhosis and can complicate medical procedures such as the placement of gastrostomy tubes due to the heightened risk of bleeding. Overall, portal hypertension is a significant concern in the management of liver-related health issues, especially in the context of cirrhosis."}{"title": "SYSTEM NATIONAL DE SALUD:The Sistema Nacional de Salud is the national health system in Spain that regulates healthcare services, including nutritional support for patients."}{"title": "MINISTERIO DE SANIDAD:The Ministerio de Sanidad, also known as the Spanish Ministry of Health, is a governmental body responsible for public health policies in Spain. It oversees health services and financing within the healthcare system, ensuring the implementation of health guidelines. Among its various responsibilities, the Ministerio de Sanidad provides guidelines for enteral nutrition and home parenteral nutrition, reflecting its commitment to managing nutritional health as part of its broader public health mandate."}{"title": "SONDA DE GASTROSTOM\u00cdA:The \"SONDA DE GASTROSTOM\u00cdA\" is a medical device designed to provide long-term nutritional support for patients who are unable to eat orally. It is inserted into the stomach through the abdominal wall, facilitating enteral nutrition. This device is particularly useful in procedures such as endoscopic gastrostomy, where it allows for direct feeding into the stomach. The gastrostomy tube can be replaced by a button once a gastrocutaneous fistula has formed, offering a more comfortable option for ongoing nutritional support. Overall, the gastrostomy tube is essential for patients who cannot maintain adequate nutritional status through oral intake."}{"title": "TUMORES DE CABEZA Y CUELLO:TUMORES DE CABEZA Y CUELLO, or head and neck tumors, are cancers located in the head and neck region that can significantly impact a patient's ability to swallow and maintain proper nutritional status. These tumors may necessitate surgical intervention, and post-surgery, patients often require specialized nutritional support to aid in their recovery. Due to the potential difficulties in swallowing, alternative feeding methods, such as gastrostomy, may be necessary. Therefore, careful nutritional assessment and support are essential for individuals affected by these medical conditions."}{"title": "FORMULAS ENTERALES:FORMULAS ENTERALES are specialized nutritional products specifically designed for enteral feeding, providing complete nutrition to patients who require this form of dietary support. These enteral formulas are particularly beneficial for surgical patients, as they help meet their nutritional needs during recovery."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULAS MONOM\u00c9RICAS:Las f\u00f3rmulas monom\u00e9ricas son soluciones que contienen amino\u00e1cidos libres y son utilizadas en la nutrici\u00f3n enteral."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULAS PEPT\u00cdDICAS:Las f\u00f3rmulas pept\u00eddicas son soluciones que predominan en p\u00e9ptidos y son utilizadas en la nutrici\u00f3n enteral."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULAS ESPEC\u00cdFICAS:F\u00f3rmulas espec\u00edficas are specialized nutritional formulas tailored for patients with specific health conditions, including diabetes and various metabolic or digestive diseases. These formulas serve as nutritional solutions that are adapted to meet the unique needs of individuals suffering from these conditions. They are designed not only to provide essential nutrients but also to influence the evolution and prognosis of certain diseases, thereby supporting the overall health and well-being of patients."}{"title": "OSMOLALIDAD:La osmolalidad es una medida de la concentraci\u00f3n de part\u00edculas osm\u00f3ticamente activas en una soluci\u00f3n, importante en la clasificaci\u00f3n de f\u00f3rmulas de nutrici\u00f3n enteral."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULAS EST\u00c1NDAR:F\u00d3RMULAS EST\u00c1NDAR se refiere a preparaciones nutricionales com\u00fanmente utilizadas que, en ciertos casos, no presentan diferencias significativas en comparaci\u00f3n con f\u00f3rmulas espec\u00edficas. Estas f\u00f3rmulas son dise\u00f1adas para proporcionar una nutrici\u00f3n adecuada y son ampliamente empleadas en diversas aplicaciones."}{"title": "F\u00d3RMULAS OLIGOMONOM\u00c9RICAS:Las f\u00f3rmulas oligomonom\u00e9ricas son productos de nutrici\u00f3n enteral en las que las prote\u00ednas se encuentran hidrolizadas en peque\u00f1os p\u00e9ptidos a amino\u00e1cidos libres, clasificadas seg\u00fan su composici\u00f3n y caracter\u00edsticas nutricionales."}{"title": "DEL OLMO GARC\u00cdA D.:Del Olmo Garc\u00eda D. es un autor que ha escrito sobre productos diet\u00e9ticos para usos nutricionales espec\u00edficos."}{"title": "DIETAS OLIGOMONOM\u00c9RICAS:Las dietas oligomonom\u00e9ricas son f\u00f3rmulas que tienen una osmolalidad moderadamente hipert\u00f3nica, entre 350-550 mOsm/kg, y son utilizadas en nutrici\u00f3n enteral."}{"title": "DIETAS MONOM\u00c9RICAS:Las dietas monom\u00e9ricas son f\u00f3rmulas con osmolalidad hipert\u00f3nica, superior a 550 mOsm/kg, utilizadas en nutrici\u00f3n enteral."}{"title": "CASE\u00cdNA:Case\u00edna is a protein found in milk that has garnered attention for its various health benefits, including potential anticancer properties. It is recognized as a slow-digesting dairy protein, making it a popular choice in nutritional supplements aimed at muscle recovery and sustained energy. Additionally, case\u00edna is utilized in nutritional products for promoting satiety, which can aid in weight management. It serves as the primary source of protein in polymeric and oligomeric formulas, available in both intact and hydrolyzed forms. Overall, case\u00edna is valued for its nutritional applications and its role in supporting muscle health and recovery."}{"title": "LACTOALB\u00daMINA:Lactoalb\u00famina is a protein derived from whey, recognized for its high biological value. It serves as a significant source of protein and is commonly utilized in various dietary supplements. Additionally, lactoalb\u00famina is incorporated into certain enteral nutrition formulas, highlighting its importance in nutritional support and supplementation."}{"title": "PROTE\u00cdNA DE SOJA:La prote\u00edna de soja es un al\u00e9rgeno que puede provocar reacciones adversas en lactantes y ni\u00f1os mayores, de manera similar a la prote\u00edna de la leche de vaca. Adem\u00e1s, se utiliza como una de las fuentes de prote\u00ednas en f\u00f3rmulas de nutrici\u00f3n enteral, lo que resalta su importancia en la alimentaci\u00f3n y nutrici\u00f3n de ciertos grupos de poblaci\u00f3n."}{"title": "PROTE\u00cdNA DEL GUISANTE:La prote\u00edna del guisante es otra fuente de prote\u00edna utilizada en f\u00f3rmulas de nutrici\u00f3n enteral."}{"title": "PROTE\u00cdNAS DE LACTOSUERO:Las prote\u00ednas de lactosuero son utilizadas en algunas f\u00f3rmulas de nutrici\u00f3n enteral como fuente de prote\u00edna."}{"title": "S\u00c1NCHEZ DE MEDINA CONTRERAS:S\u00e1nchez de Medina Contreras is the editor of the book 'Tratado de Nutrici\u00f3n', which discusses nutritional support in medical contexts."}{"title": "INSTITUTE FOR SAFE MEDICATION PRACTICES:The Institute for Safe Medication Practices (ISMP) is an organization that focuses on medication safety and includes parenteral nutrition among high-risk medications."}{"title": "BRET\u00d3N LESMES I:Bret\u00f3n Lesmes I is an author of a manual on parenteral nutrition published by the Spanish Society of Endocrinology and Nutrition."}{"title": "MOTILLA DE LA C\u00c1MARA M:Motilla de la C\u00e1mara M is an author of a manual on parenteral nutrition published by the Spanish Society of Endocrinology and Nutrition."}{"title": "CUERDA COMP\u00c9S C:Cuerda Comp\u00e9s C is an author of a manual on parenteral nutrition published by the Spanish Society of Endocrinology and Nutrition."}{"title": "GOMIS P:Gomis P is an author who specializes in the formulation and preparation of parenteral nutrition. Additionally, Gomis P is involved in the study of oral glutamine supplements specifically for hematopoietic transplant patients. This dual focus highlights Gomis P's contributions to both nutritional support and the management of patients undergoing significant medical treatments."}{"title": "INARAJA MT:Inaraja MT is an author involved in the formulation and preparation of parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "V\u00c1ZQUEZ A:V\u00e1zquez A is an author involved in the formulation and preparation of parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "MART\u00cdNEZ-V\u00c1ZQUEZ MJ:Mart\u00ednez-V\u00e1zquez MJ is an author involved in the formulation and preparation of parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "CALVO MV:Calvo MV is an author involved in the formulation and preparation of parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "OBSTRUCCI\u00d3N MEC\u00c1NICA INTESTINAL:Obstrucci\u00f3n Mec\u00e1nica Intestinal is a medical condition characterized by a blockage in the intestine that prevents the normal passage of contents. This blockage can lead to complications that may necessitate the use of parenteral nutrition, particularly when oral feeding is not feasible. The condition is recognized in both English and Spanish, highlighting its significance in medical discussions across different languages."}{"title": "ALTERACIONES DE LA MOTILIDAD INTESTINAL:\"ALTERACIONES DE LA MOTILIDAD INTESTINAL\" refers to disorders that impact the normal movement of the intestines. These conditions can significantly disrupt gastrointestinal function, potentially resulting in severe cases that necessitate parenteral nutrition. The term encompasses various issues that hinder the intestines' ability to move food and waste effectively, highlighting the critical nature of these disorders in relation to nutritional health."}{"title": "AFECTACI\u00d3N EXTENSA DE LA MUCOSA INTESTINAL:A condition where extensive damage to the intestinal lining occurs, leading to malabsorption and the potential requirement for parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "\u00c1CIDOS GRASOS \u03a9-3:\u00c1cidos Grasos \u03c9-3, commonly known as omega-3 fatty acids, are essential fats recognized for their numerous health benefits. They play a significant role in optimizing post-exercise recovery and are often utilized in conjunction with other medications to lower triglyceride levels. Omega-3 fatty acids are included in fourth-generation lipid emulsions for parenteral nutrition, where they are valued for their anti-inflammatory properties and potential to improve nutritional outcomes in patients. They are particularly noted as a first-choice treatment for individuals with severe hypertriglyceridemia, especially those who cannot use fibrates due to contraindications. The primary components of omega-3 fatty acids, such as EPA and DHA, are derived from fish oil and are administered in high doses to effectively manage hypertriglyceridemia. Overall, omega-3 fatty acids are essential for maintaining health and are integral to various therapeutic applications."}{"title": "AMINO\u00c1CIDOS:Amino\u00e1cidos are organic compounds that serve as the fundamental building blocks of proteins, playing a crucial role in various bodily functions. They are essential nutrients included in parenteral nutrition solutions to meet the protein needs of patients, particularly those undergoing dialysis or requiring nutritional support. Amino acids are vital for maintaining lean body mass, supporting protein synthesis, and facilitating muscle synthesis and energy production. Additionally, they are important for growth and development, especially in pediatric nutrition. It is noted that specific requirements for amino acids may increase during physical exercise, highlighting their significance in both health and recovery."}{"title": "GLUCONATO C\u00c1LCICO:Calcium gluconate is a form of calcium used in parenteral nutrition to avoid calculation errors associated with calcium chloride."}{"title": "F\u00cdSTULA INTESTINAL:F\u00edstula intestinal refers to an abnormal connection between the intestine and another organ or the skin. This condition can arise from various medical issues, including diseases such as cancer or complications following surgical procedures. The presence of an intestinal fistula may lead to significant health implications, including the potential for intestinal failure. In some cases, patients with this condition may require parenteral nutrition to ensure adequate nutrient delivery, as the abnormal connection can disrupt normal digestive processes. Overall, intestinal fistulas represent a serious medical concern that necessitates careful management and treatment."}{"title": "TORRES TORRES B:Torres Torres B is an author referenced in the context of parenteral nutrition and its complications."}{"title": "LOPEZ G\u00d3MEZ JJ:L\u00f3pez G\u00f3mez JJ is an author referenced in the context of parenteral nutrition and its complications."}{"title": "G\u00d3MEZ HOYOS E:G\u00f3mez Hoyos E is an author recognized for contributions to the field of parenteral nutrition and its associated complications. This author has specifically studied the effects of correcting serum sodium levels in patients undergoing parenteral nutrition, with findings presented at the 17th European Congress of Endocrinology."}{"title": "ORTOL\u00c1 BUIGES A:Ortol\u00e1 Buiges A is an author referenced in the context of parenteral nutrition and its complications."}{"title": "AULA M\u00c9DICA:Aula M\u00e9dica is a medical publishing house that specializes in producing literature related to clinical nutrition and medical guidelines. The organization is known for publishing textbooks that cover topics in clinical nutrition and metabolism, contributing to the field of medical education. Additionally, Aula M\u00e9dica is recognized as the publisher of a referenced book specifically focused on clinical nutrition and metabolism, further solidifying its role in disseminating important medical knowledge."}{"title": "\u00c1CIDOS GRASOS \u03a9-6:Omega-6 fatty acids are essential fatty acids provided by lipid emulsions, important for various bodily functions."}{"title": "ESTEATOSIS HEP\u00c1TICA:ESTEATOSIS HEP\u00c1TICA, also known as hepatic steatosis, is a medical condition characterized by the accumulation of fat in the liver. This condition is commonly observed in patients receiving parenteral nutrition, particularly after the initiation of such treatment. Additionally, hepatic steatosis can occur in patients with cystic fibrosis, where it is often associated with severe malnutrition. The condition highlights the importance of monitoring liver health in individuals undergoing parenteral nutrition and those with specific health challenges like cystic fibrosis."}{"title": "FOSFOL\u00cdPIDOS:FOSFOL\u00cdPIDOS, or phospholipids, are a class of lipids that serve as a major component of all cell membranes, playing a crucial role in maintaining cellular structure and function. They are essential for various cellular processes, including those that require copper for their synthesis. Additionally, phospholipids are included in some nutritional products, highlighting their importance not only in cellular biology but also in nutrition."}{"title": "DEL OLMO D:Del Olmo D is an author referenced in the guidelines for enteral and parenteral formulas."}{"title": "MART\u00cdN JD:Mart\u00edn JD is an author referenced in the guidelines for enteral and parenteral formulas."}{"title": "A.S.P.E.N.:A.S.P.E.N. (American Society for Parenteral and Enteral Nutrition) is an organization dedicated to providing guidelines and recommendations for nutrition support in clinical settings. It focuses on the nutritional needs of patients, particularly those with hyperglycemia, and issues clinical guidelines to ensure effective nutrition support. Additionally, A.S.P.E.N. publishes position papers on various nutritional practices, further contributing to the advancement of knowledge and standards in the field of nutrition support."}{"title": "HIPO- HIPERNATREMIA:Hypo- and hypernatremia refer to low and high sodium levels in the blood, respectively, which can occur in patients receiving parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "HIPO- HIPERPOTASEMIA:Hypo- and hyperkalemia refer to low and high potassium levels in the blood, respectively, which can occur in patients receiving parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "TABLA 5:Table 5 presents a comprehensive overview of several key aspects related to patient care and nutrition. It includes the results of a study aimed at assessing the patient's hyperglycemic syndrome, providing valuable insights into this condition. Additionally, Table 5 summarizes the hydroelectrolytic content of various secretions, which is crucial for ensuring proper supplementation in parenteral nutrition. Furthermore, it outlines the mandatory and voluntary formats for presenting nutritional information, highlighting the importance of clear communication in dietary practices. Overall, Table 5 serves as an essential resource for understanding and managing nutritional needs in clinical settings."}{"title": "STAPHYLOCOCCUS AUREUS:Staphylococcus aureus is a common bacterium known for its role in causing various infections, particularly in patients with medical devices such as catheters. It is recognized as a significant pathogen in catheter-related infections and can lead to severe conditions, including sepsis, especially in individuals with central venous catheters. Additionally, Staphylococcus aureus has been proposed to act as a trigger for low-grade inflammation, which is associated with weight gain. This dual role highlights its importance not only as a cause of infections but also in potential metabolic implications."}{"title": "CAT\u00c9TER VENOSO CENTRAL TUNELIZADO TIPO HICKMAN:The Hickman catheter is a type of central venous catheter used for long-term intravenous access, often in patients requiring parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "CULTIVOS:Cultivos refer to microbiological tests performed to identify infections, such as those caused by Staphylococcus aureus in patients with catheters."}{"title": "ETANOL:ETANOL, also known as ethanol, is a chemical compound with diverse applications and implications in both medical and recreational contexts. In medical settings, ETANOL is utilized for sealing catheters to prevent infections, highlighting its importance in maintaining sterile conditions in healthcare. However, it is also associated with potential health risks; studies have indicated that ethanol may be linked to an increased risk of thrombosis in patients receiving parenteral nutrition. Beyond its medical uses, ethanol is widely recognized as a type of alcohol found in beverages, characterized by its high energy density and consumption in various forms. This dual nature of ETANOL underscores its significance in both health-related applications and social practices."}{"title": "TAUROLIDINA:TAUROLIDINA is a compound utilized in medical settings primarily for its prophylactic properties in catheter sealing, aimed at reducing infection rates. It is particularly recommended for use in parenteral nutrition to prevent infections and complications associated with central venous catheters. Overall, TAUROLIDINA serves as an important measure in the prevention of infections linked to catheter use."}{"title": "TEDUGLUTIDE:TEDUGLUTIDE is a medication currently under investigation for the treatment of intestinal failure, specifically targeting conditions such as Short Bowel Syndrome. It works by promoting intestinal adaptation, which enhances the absorption of nutrients in the intestines. This mechanism helps to reduce the reliance on parenteral nutrition in patients suffering from intestinal failure, thereby improving their overall nutritional status and quality of life."}{"title": "MART\u00cdNEZ FAEDO C:MART\u00cdNEZ FAEDO C is an author and researcher known for their work on complications associated with home parenteral nutrition. They have conducted a referenced study that explores the various complications that can arise from this form of nutrition, contributing valuable insights to the field."}{"title": "LABORDA GONZ\u00c1LEZ L:LABORDA GONZ\u00c1LEZ L is an author of a referenced study on complications associated with home parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "VIRGILI CASAS N:VIRGILI CASAS N is an author of a referenced study on complications associated with home parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "G\u00d3MEZ ENTERR\u00cdA P:G\u00d3MEZ ENTERR\u00cdA P is an author of a referenced study on complications associated with home parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "GRUPO DE TRABAJO NADYA-SENPE:GRUPO DE TRABAJO NADYA-SENPE is a working group focused on the study of complications related to home parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "ENHANCED RECOVERY AFTER SURGERY SOCIETY:The Enhanced Recovery After Surgery Society provides guidelines for perioperative care, particularly in elective surgeries like colonic surgery."}{"title": "GUSTAFSSON UO:Gustafsson UO is an author of the guidelines for perioperative care in elective colonic surgery. He has contributed to the development of these guidelines, which are designed to improve patient outcomes during the perioperative period for elective colonic procedures."}{"title": "SCOTT MJ:Scott MJ is a contributing author to the Enhanced Recovery After Surgery Society guidelines."}{"title": "ARENDS J:Arends J is an author who has made significant contributions to the field of nutrition, particularly in relation to cancer care. They are involved in the ESPEN guidelines, which focus on chronic nutrition and specifically address enteral nutrition in non-surgical oncology. Additionally, Arends J is recognized as one of the authors of the ESPEN guidelines on nutrition for cancer patients, highlighting their expertise and commitment to improving nutritional practices in this critical area of healthcare."}{"title": "INSULINRESISTENCIA:Insulin resistance is a condition that can affect nutritional needs and management in patients, particularly those with cancer."}{"title": "EUROPEAN SOCIETY OF CLINICAL NUTRITION AND METABOLISM:The European Society of Clinical Nutrition and Metabolism (ESPEN) is an organization that develops guidelines on nutrition for various patient groups, including those with cancer and dementia."}{"title": "VITAMIN B12:Vitamin B12 is a B vitamin that is essential for various critical bodily functions, particularly in the formation of red blood cells and the maintenance of neurological health. It plays a vital role in brain function and is often discussed in relation to cognitive health, including conditions such as dementia. As a water-soluble vitamin, Vitamin B12 is important for the normal functioning of the brain and nervous system, as well as for the production of DNA. Additionally, it is crucial for nerve function and the metabolism of homocysteine, making it significant for metabolic control, especially in patients with conditions like homocystinuria. Specific recommendations for Vitamin B12 intake are often made for patients with certain health conditions, including those related to FQ (fluoroquinolone) use. Overall, Vitamin B12 is a key nutrient that supports both physical and cognitive health."}{"title": "NEFROLITIASIS:Nefrolitiasis, also known as nephrolithiasis, is a medical condition characterized by the formation of kidney stones. This condition is considered a systemic and chronic pathology that can be influenced by various dietary and environmental factors. Specifically, dietary elements such as calcium, oxalate, and purine intake play significant roles in the development of kidney stones. \n\nThe formation of these stones can be exacerbated by certain dietary practices, including those associated with hypocaloric diets, which may lead to increased calcium excretion. Additionally, individuals with specific medical conditions, such as glucose-galactose malabsorption or those with ileostomy, may face a higher risk of developing nephrolithiasis if their condition is not properly managed.\n\nManagement of nefrolitiasis often involves dietary modifications to control the intake of substances that contribute to stone formation. It is also important to note that nefrolitiasis can present contraindications for certain medications, such as fentermina and topiramato, which may complicate treatment options for affected individuals. Overall, nefrolitiasis is a multifaceted condition that requires careful consideration of dietary habits and medical history for effective management."}{"title": "SUPLEMENTACI\u00d3N ORAL NUTRICIONAL:"}{"title": "HIGUERA PULGAR I:Higuera Pulgar I is an author referenced in the context of nutrition in adults with intestinal failure."}{"title": "CUERDA COMP\u00c9S MC:Cuerda Comp\u00e9s MC is an author recognized for their contributions to the field of nutrition, particularly in the context of artificial nutrition management at home in Spain. They have written extensively on the subject, focusing on the nutritional needs of adults with intestinal failure. Their work is significant in addressing the complexities of managing nutrition in patients requiring specialized dietary interventions."}{"title": "GIL HERN\u00c1NDEZ A:Gil Hern\u00e1ndez A is an editor of the book titled 'Tratado de Nutrici\u00f3n'. He is referenced in the context of this nutrition treatise, highlighting his role in the editorial process of this significant work on nutrition."}{"title": "FONTANA GALLEGO L:Fontana Gallego L is an editor known for their work on the book 'Tratado de Nutrici\u00f3n'. They are referenced in the context of this nutrition treatise, highlighting their role in the publication and contribution to the field of nutrition."}{"title": "S\u00c1NCHEZ DE MEDINA CONTRERAS F:S\u00e1nchez de Medina Contreras F is an editor known for their work on the book 'Tratado de Nutrici\u00f3n'. They are referenced in the context of this nutrition treatise, highlighting their role in the editorial process of this significant publication."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N EN EL SIC DEL ADULTO:A chapter in a treatise discussing nutrition in adults with intestinal failure."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N ARTIFICIAL DOMICILIARIA:\"NUTRICI\u00d3N ARTIFICIAL DOMICILIARIA\" (NAD) refers to a medical intervention that provides nutritional support to patients in their own homes. This approach encompasses the administration of nutrition through enteral (NED) or parenteral (NPD) methods, aimed at improving or maintaining the nutritional status of patients who are unable to obtain adequate nutrition through oral intake. NAD is recognized as a significant advancement in the care of chronic patients, allowing them to receive necessary nutritional support without the need for hospitalization. \n\nBy enabling patients to remain in their familiar social and family environments, NAD not only enhances their nutritional status but also helps reduce potential complications associated with inadequate nutrition. The provision of nutritional support at home is documented by the Grupo NADYA-SENPE and is essential for those who cannot meet their dietary needs through natural foods. Overall, \"NUTRICI\u00d3N ARTIFICIAL DOMICILIARIA\" plays a crucial role in the management of patients requiring specialized nutritional therapy in a home setting."}{"title": "SIC:The Short Bowel Syndrome (SIC) is a medical condition characterized by the loss of a significant portion of the small intestine, resulting in the preservation of less than 115 cm of intestinal length. This condition severely impacts the absorption of nutrients, leading to nutritional deficiencies and various complications. Patients with SIC may require parenteral nutrition to maintain their health due to the insufficient intestinal length for adequate nutrient absorption. The syndrome often arises following surgical resections of the intestine, which can further exacerbate the challenges in nutrient uptake. Additionally, SIC is associated with the evaluation of intestinal anatomy and complications such as abscesses, highlighting the importance of medical organizations focused on the diagnosis and treatment of intestinal conditions."}{"title": "MORIES \u00c1LVAREZ:Mories \u00c1lvarez is an author referenced in the context of eating disorders and nutrition, contributing to the Manual de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n."}{"title": "DELAGADO G\u00d3MEZ:Delgado G\u00f3mez is an author referenced in the context of eating disorders and nutrition, contributing to the Manual de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n."}{"title": "SOCIETY OF ENDOCRINOLOGY AND NUTRITION:The Society of Endocrinology and Nutrition is a professional organization that provides guidelines and recommendations for the treatment of endocrine and nutritional disorders."}{"title": "REYES-GARC\u00cdA:Reyes-Garc\u00eda is an author referenced in the context of osteoporosis and mineral metabolism, contributing to the update on recommendations for the evaluation and treatment of osteoporosis."}{"title": "GARC\u00cdA-MART\u00cdN:Garc\u00eda-Mart\u00edn is an author referenced in the context of osteoporosis and mineral metabolism, contributing to the update on recommendations for the evaluation and treatment of osteoporosis."}{"title": "GRUPO DE TRABAJO DE OSTEOPOROSIS Y METABOLISMO MINERAL:The Working Group on Osteoporosis and Mineral Metabolism is a group within the Society of Endocrinology and Nutrition that focuses on osteoporosis and related conditions."}{"title": "MINISTERIO DE SANIDAD Y CONSUMO:The \"MINISTERIO DE SANIDAD Y CONSUMO\" is the governmental body in Spain tasked with regulating and ensuring public health. This ministry is responsible for the creation of the National Registry of Advance Directives and oversees public health policies and guidelines, which encompass various areas including mental health and eating disorders. Additionally, the ministry plays a role in consumer protection and provides access to Cochrane reviews in Spanish, further supporting its commitment to public health and informed consumer choices."}{"title": "GU\u00cdA DE PR\u00c1CTICA CL\u00cdNICA SOBRE TRASTORNOS DE LA CONDUCTA ALIMENTARIA:The Clinical Practice Guide on Eating Disorders is a guideline published to assist in the management and treatment of eating disorders in Spain."}{"title": "DHEA-S:DHEA-S (Dehydroepiandrosterone sulfate) is a hormone produced by the adrenal glands, playing a significant role in various physiological processes. It is often measured to assess adrenal function, particularly in the context of hyperandrogenism and conditions such as Polycystic Ovary Syndrome. Normal levels of DHEA-S can be crucial for evaluating the malignancy of adrenal lesions, as it serves as a controversial marker in the study of adrenal incidentalomas, indicating malignancy with greater specificity than sensitivity.\n\nIn addition to its role in adrenal function, DHEA-S levels can be altered in individuals with eating disorders, highlighting its importance in metabolic health. The hormone is also noted to decrease with age, and lower levels have been associated with fragility and loss of muscle mass. Furthermore, DHEA-S is measured in relation to early puberty, underscoring its relevance in developmental processes. Overall, DHEA-S is a multifaceted hormone that provides valuable insights into adrenal health and various clinical conditions."}{"title": "HIPERCORTISOLISMO:HIPERCORTISOLISMO is a condition characterized by excessive cortisol production in the body. This condition is often evaluated in patients with adrenal incidentalomas, which are unexpected findings of adrenal masses during imaging studies. Additionally, hypercortisolism can occur in individuals with eating disorders, highlighting its potential association with various health issues. The diagnosis and assessment of hypercortisolism typically involve hormonal testing to measure cortisol levels, providing a comprehensive evaluation of the patient's hormonal status."}{"title": "AUTOAGRESI\u00d3N:Autoagresi\u00f3n refers to self-harming behaviors that can occur in individuals with eating disorders, often as a coping mechanism for emotional distress."}{"title": "LESIONES ORODENTALES:Lesiones orodentales are oral and dental injuries that can occur in individuals with eating disorders, often due to behaviors such as vomiting."}{"title": "EROSIONES DENTALES:Erosiones dentales are dental erosions that can occur in individuals with eating disorders, particularly those who engage in purging behaviors."}{"title": "DESMINERALIZACIONES DEL ESMALTE:Desmineralizaciones del esmalte refers to the loss of minerals from tooth enamel, which can occur in individuals with eating disorders due to poor nutrition and acid exposure from vomiting."}{"title": "CORTES:Cortes are cuts that may be self-inflicted by individuals with eating disorders as a form of self-harm."}{"title": "ARA\u00d1AZOS:Ara\u00f1azos are scratches that may be self-inflicted by individuals with eating disorders as a form of self-harm."}{"title": "HIPOGLUCEMIA INSUL\u00cdNICA:Hipoglucemia insul\u00ednica is a condition that can occur when insulin levels are high relative to glucose levels, often discussed in the context of metabolic responses in eating disorders."}{"title": "DIABETES INS\u00cdPIDA PARCIAL:Diabetes ins\u00edpida parcial is a condition that can affect water balance in the body, potentially relevant in the context of eating disorders.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "DSM-IV:The DSM-IV is a manual published by the American Psychiatric Association that outlines the criteria for diagnosing mental disorders, including anorexia nerviosa."}{"title": "DSM-5:The DSM-5, or the Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders, Fifth Edition, is a comprehensive manual that provides standardized criteria for the classification and diagnosis of mental health conditions. It serves as an essential resource for mental health professionals, offering detailed criteria for diagnosing various disorders, including eating disorders such as anorexia nervosa and bulimia nerviosa. The DSM-5 is the updated version of the previous edition, DSM-IV, and includes revised criteria that reflect the latest research and understanding of mental health conditions. Overall, the DSM-5 plays a crucial role in the field of mental health by standardizing the diagnostic process and improving the accuracy of mental health assessments."}{"title": "GRUPO DE TRABAJO DE LA GU\u00cdA DE PR\u00c1CTICA CL\u00cdNICA:This group is responsible for developing clinical practice guidelines on eating disorders in Spain, including anorexia nerviosa."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME DE WERNICKE-KORSAKOFF:Wernicke-Korsakoff syndrome is a neurological disorder caused by thiamine deficiency, often associated with chronic alcoholism and malnutrition, leading to confusion and memory issues."}{"title": "EDUCACI\u00d3N NUTRICIONAL:\"Educaci\u00f3n nutricional\" refers to the process of educating patients about proper dietary practices to manage their health conditions, particularly diabetes. It encompasses teaching individuals about healthy eating habits and the significance of nutrition in maintaining overall health and preventing diseases. Additionally, nutritional education plays a crucial role in the treatment of patients with eating disorders, as it helps them understand and adopt healthy eating patterns. Overall, educaci\u00f3n nutricional is essential for promoting better health outcomes through informed dietary choices."}{"title": "BULIMIA NERVIOSA:Bulimia Nervosa (BN) is an eating disorder characterized by recurrent episodes of binge eating, during which individuals consume large quantities of food in a short period. This behavior is typically followed by inappropriate compensatory actions aimed at preventing weight gain, such as self-induced vomiting, excessive exercise, or the misuse of laxatives. The disorder can lead to a range of serious health complications and often goes unnoticed by those around the affected individual. Treatment for Bulimia Nervosa generally requires a multifaceted approach that includes psychotherapy and medication to address both the psychological and physical aspects of the disorder."}{"title": "AG\u00c8NCIA D'AVALUACI\u00d3 DE TECNOLOGIA I RECERCA M\u00c8DIQUES DE CATALUNYA:The Agency for Health Technology Assessment and Research in Catalonia evaluates medical technologies and provides guidelines for health practices."}{"title": "PELEGRINA CORT\u00c9S B:Pelegrina Cort\u00e9s B is an author who contributed to the chapter on nutrition in eating disorders in a medical textbook."}{"title": "PALMA MILLA S:Palma Milla S is an author who contributed to the chapter on nutrition in eating disorders in a medical textbook."}{"title": "TOMOS V:Tomo V is a volume of a medical textbook that includes a chapter on nutrition in eating disorders."}{"title": "TOPIRAMATO:Topiramate, also known as Topiramato, is a versatile medication primarily used for the prevention of seizures and migraine management. In addition to its neurological applications, Topiramate has demonstrated effectiveness in addressing uncontrolled eating and related psychological issues in patients with eating disorders. It is particularly noted for its appetite-suppressing properties. When combined with fentermina, Topiramate is indicated for weight loss in patients who have not met their weight loss goals with lower doses. This combination therapy has received approval from the FDA for the treatment of obesity, although it has not been approved by the EMA. Furthermore, there are considerations regarding Topiramate's potential effects on kidney stone formation, which is an important aspect to monitor during treatment."}{"title": "METOTREXATO:Methotrexate, known as Metotrexato, is a medication that serves as a chemotherapy agent and immune system suppressant, primarily used in the treatment of cancer and autoimmune diseases. Its mechanism of action involves the inhibition of folate reductase, which can lead to a deficiency of folic acid and may contribute to anemia, particularly in patients with inflammatory bowel disease. Additionally, Methotrexate is classified as a cytotoxic agent that interacts pharmacokinetically with glutamine, potentially enhancing its intratumoral concentrations and therapeutic effects."}{"title": "ISONIACIDA:Isoniazid is a medication that can cause a deficiency of vitamin B6 due to malabsorption."}{"title": "COLESTIRAMINA:Colestiramina, also known as Cholestyramine, is a medication that is primarily used to help control cholesterol levels in patients. However, it is important to note that the use of Colestiramina can lead to malabsorption of fat-soluble vitamins and other nutrients, which may have implications for the patient's overall nutritional status."}{"title": "LUIS DA:Luis DA is an editor and contributor to the book 'Dietoterapia, nutrici\u00f3n cl\u00ednica y metabolismo'."}{"title": "BELLIDO GUERRERO D:Bellido Guerrero D is an editor and contributor to the book 'Dietoterapia, nutrici\u00f3n cl\u00ednica y metabolismo'."}{"title": "GARC\u00cdA LUNA PP:Garc\u00eda Luna PP is an editor and contributor to the book titled 'Dietoterapia, nutrici\u00f3n cl\u00ednica y metabolismo.'"}{"title": "EFSA:The European Food Safety Authority (EFSA) is an agency dedicated to providing scientific advice on food safety and nutrition within the European Union. It plays a crucial role in assessing risks associated with the food chain, including specific recommendations on the consumption of substances such as methylmercury. EFSA also offers scientific guidance on dietary reference values for fats and fatty acids, ensuring that nutritional standards are based on sound research. Additionally, the agency evaluates health claims related to very low calorie diets, contributing to informed decision-making regarding dietary supplements and overall food safety."}{"title": "VLCD:The Very Low Calorie Diet (VLCD) is a dietary regimen characterized by a caloric intake of less than 12 kcal/kg of ideal body weight per day, typically ranging between 450 and 800 kcal daily. This approach is primarily utilized for significant weight loss, particularly in obese patients, and is often implemented as a preparatory measure before bariatric surgery. VLCDs involve substituting one or more meals with low-calorie formulas, which usually provide around 200 kcal per serving. The primary goal of VLCDs is to facilitate short-term weight loss, reduce liver size, and improve health conditions associated with obesity."}{"title": "BRESSON J-L:Bresson J-L is a contributor to the EFSA Panel on Dietetic Products, Nutrition and Allergies, providing expertise on dietary health claims."}{"title": "FAIRWEATHER-TAIT S:Fairweather-Tait S is a contributor to the EFSA Panel on Dietetic Products, Nutrition and Allergies, providing expertise on dietary health claims."}{"title": "FLYNN A:Flynn A is a contributor to the EFSA Panel on Dietetic Products, Nutrition and Allergies, providing expertise on dietary health claims."}{"title": "GOLLY I:Golly I is a contributor to the EFSA Panel on Dietetic Products, Nutrition and Allergies, providing expertise on dietary health claims."}{"title": "KORHONEN H:Korhonen H is a contributor to the EFSA Panel on Dietetic Products, Nutrition and Allergies, providing expertise on dietary health claims."}{"title": "CALLEJA FERN\u00c1NDEZ A:Calleja Fern\u00e1ndez A is a contributor to the book 'Dietoterapia, nutrici\u00f3n cl\u00ednica y metabolismo', focusing on dietary treatment of obesity."}{"title": "KYRIAKOS G:Kyriakos G is a contributor to the book 'Dietoterapia, nutrici\u00f3n cl\u00ednica y metabolismo', focusing on dietary treatment of obesity."}{"title": "VILLAR TAIBO R:Villar Taibo R is a contributor to the book 'Dietoterapia, nutrici\u00f3n cl\u00ednica y metabolismo', focusing on dietary treatment of obesity."}{"title": "AGOSTONI C:"}{"title": "SEH-LELHA:SEH-LELHA is an organization dedicated to promoting health and wellness through various initiatives. It offers a food table and nutritional composition calculator as part of its comprehensive nutrition program, which aids individuals in understanding their dietary intake. Additionally, SEH-LELHA provides guidelines for physical exercise prescription specifically tailored for patients with cardiovascular risk, emphasizing the importance of physical activity in managing health. As a scientific society, the Sociedad Espa\u00f1ola de Hipertensi\u00f3n Arterial (SEH-LELHA) also offers online tools for dietary intake calculations and nutritional analysis, further supporting individuals in making informed dietary choices."}{"title": "FENILCETONURIA:Fenilcetonuria, also known as phenylketonuria (PKU), is a metabolic disorder characterized by high levels of phenylalanine in the blood due to a deficiency in the enzyme phenylalanine hydroxylase (PAH). This condition requires lifelong dietary management to control phenylalanine levels in the body, as excessive accumulation can lead to serious health issues, including intellectual disability and malformations in fetuses of mothers with elevated phenylalanine levels during pregnancy. Fenilcetonuria is recognized as the most common inherited metabolic disorder resulting from this enzymatic deficiency, necessitating careful monitoring and dietary restrictions to prevent toxic effects associated with phenylalanine accumulation."}{"title": "TETRAHIDROBIOPTERINA:TETRAHIDROBIOPTERINA, also known as tetrahydrobiopterin (BH4), is a crucial cofactor for the hydroxylases of phenylalanine, tyrosine, and tryptophan. It plays a significant role in the treatment of mild phenylketonuria, a metabolic disorder that affects the body's ability to process phenylalanine. Tetrahydrobiopterin can enhance tolerance to phenylalanine in patients suffering from this condition, thereby aiding in the management of their dietary restrictions and overall health."}{"title": "ALIMENTOS RICOS EN FENILALANINA:Foods high in phenylalanine include meats, fish, eggs, cheese, nuts, soy, and aspartame, which must be restricted in the diet of affected individuals."}{"title": "MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL:The \"MICROBIOTA INTESTINAL\" refers to the complex community of microorganisms residing in the human digestive tract, which plays a vital role in health and disease. This intestinal microbiota is crucial for various metabolic processes, including energy absorption, appetite regulation, and the maintenance of the immune system. It has been identified as a key factor in the development of metabolic disorders such as obesity and diabetes.\n\nResearch indicates that the composition and variations of the intestinal microbiota can significantly differ between Western and Eastern populations, influenced by dietary patterns. Diets rich in animal protein can alter the microbiota's composition, highlighting the relationship between diet and microbial communities in the gut. Additionally, the microbiota undergoes significant changes during early life, influenced by factors such as the method of birth and dietary intake.\n\nOverall, the intestinal microbiota is essential for energy homeostasis and has profound implications for human health, particularly in relation to metabolic conditions."}{"title": "HYPERPHENYLALANINEMIA:Hyperphenylalaninemia is a clinical condition characterized by elevated levels of phenylalanine in the blood, often due to a metabolic defect."}{"title": "AMINO\u00c1CIDOS EXENTOS DE FENILALANINA:Commercial preparations of amino acids free of phenylalanine are used for supplementation in patients with phenylketonuria."}ñg1␀␀␀␀␀Kh1␀␀␀␀␀Ii1␀␀␀␀␀j1␀␀␀␀␀∆m1␀␀␀␀␀uo1␀␀␀␀␀Úo1␀␀␀␀␀—q1␀␀␀␀␀Vr1␀␀␀␀␀t1␀␀␀␀␀Av1␀␀␀␀␀„w1␀␀␀␀␀Az1␀␀␀␀␀ä}1␀␀␀␀␀&~1␀␀␀␀␀‘~1␀␀␀␀␀\1␀␀␀␀␀'Ä1␀␀␀␀␀{Ç1␀␀␀␀␀NÉ1␀␀␀␀␀pÉ1␀␀␀␀␀Ñ1␀␀␀␀␀ØÑ1␀␀␀␀␀GÖ1␀␀␀␀␀†Ü1␀␀␀␀␀Gá1␀␀␀␀␀€á1␀␀␀␀␀%ã1␀␀␀␀␀øå1␀␀␀␀␀Uç1␀␀␀␀␀␀é1␀␀␀␀␀ãé1␀␀␀␀␀è1␀␀␀␀␀Ïë1␀␀␀␀␀í1␀␀␀␀␀sî1␀␀␀␀␀Ÿï1␀␀␀␀␀Zó1␀␀␀␀␀dô1␀␀␀␀␀ ö1␀␀␀␀␀zö1␀␀␀␀␀⁄ö1␀␀␀␀␀[õ1␀␀␀␀␀÷õ1␀␀␀␀␀âú1␀␀␀␀␀æú1␀␀␀␀␀û1␀␀␀␀␀Áû1␀␀␀␀␀ü1␀␀␀␀␀‹ü1␀␀␀␀␀∞†1␀␀␀␀␀f°1␀␀␀␀␀D£1␀␀␀␀␀§1␀␀␀␀␀°§1␀␀␀␀␀m•1␀␀␀␀␀∆ß1␀␀␀␀␀U®1␀␀␀␀␀w´1␀␀␀␀␀-¨1␀␀␀␀␀˜¨1␀␀␀␀␀›≠1␀␀␀␀␀D∞1␀␀␀␀␀≤±1␀␀␀␀␀N≤1␀␀␀␀␀‚≤1␀␀␀␀␀r≥1␀␀␀␀␀âµ1␀␀␀␀␀*∂1␀␀␀␀␀”∂1␀␀␀␀␀~∑1␀␀␀␀␀%∏1␀␀␀␀␀ô∏1␀␀␀␀␀π1␀␀␀␀␀,ª1␀␀␀␀␀üª1␀␀␀␀␀º1␀␀␀␀␀Ω1␀␀␀␀␀gæ1␀␀␀␀␀…¿1␀␀␀␀␀F¡1␀␀␀␀␀€¡1␀␀␀␀␀Íƒ1␀␀␀␀␀8«1␀␀␀␀␀Ô…1␀␀␀␀␀ÈÀ1␀␀␀␀␀ÓÕ1␀␀␀␀␀ÑŒ1␀␀␀␀␀œ1␀␀␀␀␀óœ1␀␀␀␀␀.–1␀␀␀␀␀∑–1␀␀␀␀␀@—1␀␀␀␀␀√—1␀␀␀␀␀b”1␀␀␀␀␀‘1␀␀␀␀␀ö‘1␀␀␀␀␀!’1␀␀␀␀␀ù’1␀␀␀␀␀÷1␀␀␀␀␀p÷1␀␀␀␀␀$◊1␀␀␀␀␀∫◊1␀␀␀␀␀.ÿ1␀␀␀␀␀øÿ1␀␀␀␀␀/Ÿ1␀␀␀␀␀z⁄1␀␀␀␀␀‹1␀␀␀␀␀ﬁ1␀␀␀␀␀¥ﬁ1␀␀␀␀␀*ﬂ1␀␀␀␀␀èﬂ1␀␀␀␀␀ˇﬂ1␀␀␀␀␀‡1␀␀␀␀␀º·1␀␀␀␀␀y‚1␀␀␀␀␀2„1␀␀␀␀␀‹„1␀␀␀␀␀z‰1␀␀␀␀␀	Â1␀␀␀␀␀∂Â1␀␀␀␀␀È1␀␀␀␀␀*È1␀␀␀␀␀˚È1␀␀␀␀␀µÍ1␀␀␀␀␀fÎ1␀␀␀␀␀ÓÎ1␀␀␀␀␀iÌ1␀␀␀␀␀:Ô1␀␀␀␀␀g1␀␀␀␀␀(Ò1␀␀␀␀␀∂Ò1␀␀␀␀␀9Ú1␀␀␀␀␀œÚ1␀␀␀␀␀’Ù1␀␀␀␀␀|ı1␀␀␀␀␀ˆ1␀␀␀␀␀°ˆ1␀␀␀␀␀3˜1␀␀␀␀␀…˜1␀␀␀␀␀∑˘1␀␀␀␀␀q˙1␀␀␀␀␀¸˙1␀␀␀␀␀¡˚1␀␀␀␀␀#˛1␀␀␀␀␀Íˇ1␀␀␀␀␀ü2␀␀␀␀␀2␀␀␀␀␀*2␀␀␀␀␀;2␀␀␀␀␀◊2␀␀␀␀␀Y2␀␀␀␀␀2␀␀␀␀␀≈2␀␀␀␀␀ç	2␀␀␀␀␀2␀␀␀␀␀∏2␀␀␀␀␀æ2␀␀␀␀␀2␀␀␀␀␀”2␀␀␀␀␀¢2␀␀␀␀␀82␀␀␀␀␀ﬁ2␀␀␀␀␀·2␀␀␀␀␀^2␀␀␀␀␀Ï2␀␀␀␀␀Ü2␀␀␀␀␀2␀␀␀␀␀√2␀␀␀␀␀À2␀␀␀␀␀2␀␀␀␀␀:2␀␀␀␀␀\2␀␀␀␀␀2␀␀␀␀␀œ2␀␀␀␀␀y!2␀␀␀␀␀À"2␀␀␀␀␀ñ#2␀␀␀␀␀c$2␀␀␀␀␀.%2␀␀␀␀␀˝%2␀␀␀␀␀»&2␀␀␀␀␀j'2␀␀␀␀␀˝'2␀␀␀␀␀¶(2␀␀␀␀␀≤,2␀␀␀␀␀k-2␀␀␀␀␀.2␀␀␀␀␀û.2␀␀␀␀␀°